WEBVTT

00:00:02.152 --> 00:00:05.781
That was an incredible program.

00:00:05.822 --> 00:00:07.881
I am glad you approve.

00:00:07.925 --> 00:00:09.893
I have always found
the Black Sea at night

00:00:09.927 --> 00:00:13.055
to be a most stimulating
experience.

00:00:13.096 --> 00:00:17.226
Worf, we were walking
barefoot on the beach

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:18.632
with balalaika music in the air

00:00:18.669 --> 00:00:22.264
ocean breeze washing over us

00:00:22.306 --> 00:00:26.037
stars in the sky,
a full moon rising

00:00:26.076 --> 00:00:29.273
and the most you can say
is "stimulating"?

00:00:29.313 --> 00:00:33.374
It was...

00:00:33.417 --> 00:00:35.180
very stimulating.

00:00:36.453 --> 00:00:38.546
What?

00:00:38.588 --> 00:00:39.748
You know, I don't spend

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:41.553
nearly enough time
on the holodeck.

00:00:41.591 --> 00:00:45.220
I should take my own advice
and go there to relax.

00:00:45.262 --> 00:00:47.560
Next time, I'll choose
the program.

00:00:47.597 --> 00:00:49.724
If you liked the Black Sea

00:00:49.766 --> 00:00:52.735
you're going to love
Lake Cataria on Betazed.

00:00:52.769 --> 00:00:55.738
Deanna, perhaps before
there is a next time

00:00:55.772 --> 00:00:57.899
we should discuss
Commander Riker.

00:00:57.941 --> 00:00:59.932
Why, is he coming along?

00:00:59.977 --> 00:01:01.171
No

00:01:01.211 --> 00:01:03.441
but I do not wish...

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.846
I mean, it would be
unfortunate if he...

00:01:05.882 --> 00:01:09.010
If you and I are going
to continue

00:01:09.052 --> 00:01:11.452
I do not wish
to hurt his feelings.

00:01:11.488 --> 00:01:16.152
Worf, I think it's all right
to concentrate on our feelings...

00:01:16.193 --> 00:01:18.184
yours and mine.

00:01:22.432 --> 00:01:25.333
Counselor...

00:01:25.369 --> 00:01:27.667
what's today's date?

00:01:27.704 --> 00:01:29.001
The date.

00:01:29.039 --> 00:01:30.506
Stardate 47988.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:33.100
47988.

00:01:33.143 --> 00:01:35.043
Captain, what's wrong?

00:01:35.078 --> 00:01:37.546
47988.

00:01:37.581 --> 00:01:39.549
I'm not sure.

00:01:39.583 --> 00:01:42.711
I don't know... how or why

00:01:42.753 --> 00:01:48.589
but... I'm moving
back and forth through time.

00:02:22.625 --> 00:02:27.028
Space, the final frontier.

00:02:27.063 --> 00:02:30.897
These are the voyages
of the Starship Enterprise.

00:02:30.933 --> 00:02:32.901
Its continuing mission...

00:02:32.935 --> 00:02:36.871
to explore strange new worlds

00:02:36.906 --> 00:02:41.343
to seek out new life
and new civilizations

00:02:41.377 --> 00:02:45.871
to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

00:03:47.942 --> 00:03:51.400
I had this feeling that I'd
physically left the Enterprise.

00:03:51.446 --> 00:03:53.914
I was in another time,
another place.

00:03:53.948 --> 00:03:55.916
I was somewhere in the past.

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:57.918
Can you describe where you were?

00:03:57.952 --> 00:03:59.419
What it looked like?

00:03:59.454 --> 00:04:02.355
You see, it's all
slipping away so fast.

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:03.857
I-It's like...

00:04:03.891 --> 00:04:06.519
it's like waking up
from a nightmare.

00:04:06.561 --> 00:04:09.359
I, uh...

00:04:09.397 --> 00:04:11.058
It was years ago.

00:04:11.099 --> 00:04:15.126
I-I-It was before I took command
of the Enterprise.

00:04:15.169 --> 00:04:17.000
I was talking to someone.

00:04:17.038 --> 00:04:18.562
I can't remember who.

00:04:18.606 --> 00:04:20.836
And then it all changed.

00:04:20.875 --> 00:04:23.469
I was no longer in the past.

00:04:23.511 --> 00:04:26.605
I was now... I was now
an old man in the future.

00:04:26.648 --> 00:04:31.108
And... I was outside,
and I was doing something.

00:04:35.123 --> 00:04:38.524
I can't remember what it was.

00:04:40.828 --> 00:04:42.295
I'm sorry.

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:43.888
It's, it's all gone.

00:04:43.998 --> 00:04:45.625
I just can't remember.

00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:47.134
It's all right.

00:04:47.168 --> 00:04:49.193
Have you considered
the possibility

00:04:49.237 --> 00:04:51.205
that this was just a dream?

00:04:51.239 --> 00:04:52.536
It... No, no.

00:04:52.573 --> 00:04:55.269
It was much more than a dream.

00:04:55.309 --> 00:04:57.641
The-the smells, the sounds...

00:04:57.679 --> 00:05:01.137
the, the very touch of things...

00:05:01.182 --> 00:05:03.650
much more real than a dream.

00:05:03.685 --> 00:05:06.745
How long did you spend
in each time period?

00:05:06.788 --> 00:05:08.756
Did it seem like minutes?

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:10.587
Hours?

00:05:10.625 --> 00:05:13.093
You see, I can't say.

00:05:13.127 --> 00:05:14.992
At first, I had a sense of...

00:05:15.029 --> 00:05:17.395
a sense of confusion,
disorientation.

00:05:17.432 --> 00:05:19.059
I wasn't sure where I was.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:21.261
And then all of that passed

00:05:21.302 --> 00:05:24.169
and it all seemed
perfectly natural

00:05:24.205 --> 00:05:28.437
as though I belonged
in that time.

00:05:28.476 --> 00:05:30.637
But... I can't...

00:05:48.796 --> 00:05:51.993
Captain Picard to the Bridge.

00:05:52.033 --> 00:05:53.762
Captain, we've got a problem

00:05:53.801 --> 00:05:56.292
with the warp core
or the phase inducers

00:05:56.337 --> 00:05:59.898
or some other damn thing.

00:05:59.974 --> 00:06:02.374
Geordi.

00:06:04.145 --> 00:06:05.612
Hello, Captain.

00:06:05.646 --> 00:06:07.409
Or should I call you Ambassador?

00:06:07.448 --> 00:06:11.509
Oh, I haven't been called that
for some time, either.

00:06:11.552 --> 00:06:13.486
How about "Mr. Picard"?

00:06:13.521 --> 00:06:15.318
How about "Jean-Luc"?

00:06:15.356 --> 00:06:18.814
I don't think I could
get used to that.

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:20.851
Good Lord, Geordi.

00:06:20.895 --> 00:06:25.025
Well... how long has it been?

00:06:25.066 --> 00:06:26.260
Nine years.

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:28.359
No, no, no, since you
last called me Captain...

00:06:28.402 --> 00:06:31.530
since we were all together
on the Enterprise.

00:06:31.572 --> 00:06:33.563
Close to 25 years.

00:06:33.608 --> 00:06:36.076
25 years.

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:38.806
Well, time has been good to you.

00:06:38.846 --> 00:06:41.815
A little too good
in some places.

00:06:41.849 --> 00:06:43.817
Can I give you a hand here?

00:06:43.851 --> 00:06:45.751
Oh, well, I'm, uh...

00:06:45.787 --> 00:06:48.620
I'm just tying up some vines.

00:06:59.801 --> 00:07:03.100
Mmm, you've got leaf miners.

00:07:03.137 --> 00:07:05.765
You might want to try
a bacillus spray.

00:07:05.807 --> 00:07:08.105
My wife is quite a gardener.

00:07:08.142 --> 00:07:10.838
I've picked up
a little bit of it.

00:07:10.878 --> 00:07:12.345
How is Leah?

00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:14.439
Just wonderful, busy as ever.

00:07:14.482 --> 00:07:18.043
She's just been made director
of the Daystrom Institute.

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:22.018
What about the little ones...

00:07:22.056 --> 00:07:24.786
Brett, Alandra, and, um...?

00:07:24.826 --> 00:07:25.793
Sydney.

00:07:25.827 --> 00:07:26.794
Sydney.

00:07:26.828 --> 00:07:27.988
Yeah.

00:07:28.029 --> 00:07:29.792
Well, they're not
so little anymore.

00:07:29.831 --> 00:07:31.458
Brett is applying
to Starfleet Academy

00:07:31.499 --> 00:07:34.093
next year.

00:07:36.103 --> 00:07:37.968
So, what brings you here?

00:07:38.005 --> 00:07:40.530
Oh, I just thought I'd stop by.

00:07:40.575 --> 00:07:44.978
Been thinking about
the old days on the Enterprise.

00:07:45.012 --> 00:07:46.877
I was in the neighborhood.

00:07:46.948 --> 00:07:48.279
Geordi...

00:07:48.316 --> 00:07:51.149
you don't make the trip
from Rigel III to Earth

00:07:51.185 --> 00:07:53.016
just to drop by.

00:07:55.056 --> 00:07:56.887
No.

00:07:56.991 --> 00:07:58.891
So...

00:07:58.993 --> 00:08:00.893
you heard.

00:08:00.928 --> 00:08:04.830
Leah's got a few friends
at Starfleet Medical.

00:08:04.899 --> 00:08:06.366
Word gets around.

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:08.425
I'm not an invalid.

00:08:08.469 --> 00:08:12.667
Irumodic Syndrome can take years
to run its course.

00:08:12.707 --> 00:08:14.504
I know.

00:08:14.542 --> 00:08:16.271
But once I heard...

00:08:16.310 --> 00:08:19.279
well, I just wanted
to stop by, just the same.

00:08:19.313 --> 00:08:21.281
Well, now that you're here

00:08:21.315 --> 00:08:23.715
you can help me carry
those tools.

00:08:32.593 --> 00:08:36.552
Well, my cooking may not
be up to Leah's standards

00:08:36.597 --> 00:08:39.725
but I can still make
a decent cup of tea.

00:08:39.767 --> 00:08:42.235
Oh, I read your last novel.

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:44.830
I thought that, uh,
the protagonist

00:08:44.872 --> 00:08:46.863
was a little too flamboyant

00:08:46.974 --> 00:08:48.805
but for the rest, I...

00:08:58.986 --> 00:09:01.648
Captain, are you all right?

00:09:03.391 --> 00:09:04.688
Captain!

00:09:04.725 --> 00:09:06.818
Captain?

00:09:06.928 --> 00:09:11.831
Will this be your first time
on a Galaxy-class starship?

00:09:11.933 --> 00:09:14.401
Are you all right, sir?

00:09:14.435 --> 00:09:16.062
Sir?

00:09:18.072 --> 00:09:20.040
I'm... I'm sorry, Lieutenant.

00:09:20.074 --> 00:09:22.042
My mind must have wandered.

00:09:22.076 --> 00:09:23.543
What were you saying?

00:09:23.577 --> 00:09:26.045
I was asking if you'd ever been

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:29.049
aboard a Galaxy-class
starship before.

00:09:29.083 --> 00:09:31.051
No.

00:09:31.085 --> 00:09:33.553
Of course, I'm familiar
with the blueprints

00:09:33.587 --> 00:09:35.214
and the specifications

00:09:35.256 --> 00:09:38.225
but this will be
my first time on board.

00:09:38.259 --> 00:09:41.228
Well, then, if I
may be so bold, sir

00:09:41.262 --> 00:09:42.957
you're in for a treat.

00:09:42.997 --> 00:09:45.158
The Enterprise is quite a ship.

00:09:45.199 --> 00:09:48.566
I'm sure she is.

00:09:50.571 --> 00:09:53.233
Have I done something wrong,
sir?

00:09:53.274 --> 00:09:55.401
No.

00:09:55.443 --> 00:09:58.810
It's just that you look
very familiar.

00:09:58.846 --> 00:10:01.076
Enterprise
to Shuttlecraft Galileo.

00:10:01.115 --> 00:10:03.083
You are cleared for arrival

00:10:03.117 --> 00:10:05.585
in Shuttle Bay Two.

00:10:05.619 --> 00:10:08.247
Acknowledged, Enterprise.

00:10:08.289 --> 00:10:10.757
And there she is.

00:10:26.607 --> 00:10:28.598
Captain?

00:10:35.149 --> 00:10:37.140
Captain?

00:10:40.554 --> 00:10:43.182
Tasha.

00:10:43.224 --> 00:10:46.557
I was just with Tasha
in the shuttle.

00:11:04.311 --> 00:11:06.211
I just finished
the neurographic scan.

00:11:06.246 --> 00:11:09.613
I didn't find anything that
would cause hallucinations

00:11:09.650 --> 00:11:11.311
or a psychogenic reaction.

00:11:11.351 --> 00:11:14.047
Is there any indication
of temporal displacement?

00:11:14.087 --> 00:11:16.555
No. Usually, a temporal
shift would leave some sort

00:11:16.590 --> 00:11:18.649
of tripamine residue
in the cerebral cortex

00:11:18.692 --> 00:11:20.091
but the scan didn't show any.

00:11:20.127 --> 00:11:22.687
Personally, I think you just
enjoy waking everybody up

00:11:22.729 --> 00:11:24.390
in the middle of the night.

00:11:24.431 --> 00:11:25.728
Actually, I really like

00:11:25.766 --> 00:11:28.064
running around the ship
in my bare feet.

00:11:30.337 --> 00:11:33.067
The biospectral
test results, Doctor.

00:11:34.942 --> 00:11:37.843
Your blood gas analysis
is consistent with someone

00:11:37.878 --> 00:11:40.574
who's been breathing
the ship's air for weeks.

00:11:40.614 --> 00:11:42.138
If you'd been anywhere else

00:11:42.182 --> 00:11:44.810
there would have been
an indication of change

00:11:44.851 --> 00:11:47.115
in the oxygen isotope ratios.

00:11:47.154 --> 00:11:49.315
Thanks.

00:11:49.356 --> 00:11:51.916
Deanna, would you
excuse us, please?

00:11:52.025 --> 00:11:54.516
Of course.

00:11:58.098 --> 00:12:00.566
Jean-Luc, I scanned you

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:02.761
for evidence
of Irumodic Syndrome

00:12:02.803 --> 00:12:04.100
as you suggested.

00:12:04.137 --> 00:12:06.970
There wasn't any.

00:12:07.007 --> 00:12:08.975
But I did find

00:12:09.009 --> 00:12:12.536
a small structural defect
in the parietal lobe.

00:12:14.548 --> 00:12:17.346
A defect that you
hadn't noticed before?

00:12:17.384 --> 00:12:20.512
It's the kind of defect
that would only show up

00:12:20.554 --> 00:12:22.579
on a level-4 neurographic scan

00:12:22.622 --> 00:12:26.353
that could cause you to be
susceptible to several kinds

00:12:26.393 --> 00:12:29.021
of neurological disorders,
including Irumodic Syndrome.

00:12:29.062 --> 00:12:31.622
Now, it's possible for you
to live with this defect

00:12:31.665 --> 00:12:34.691
for the rest of your life
without developing a problem.

00:12:34.735 --> 00:12:36.896
Or even if you do,
many people continue

00:12:36.937 --> 00:12:38.905
to live normal lives
for a long time

00:12:38.972 --> 00:12:41.031
after the onset
of Irumodic Syndrome.

00:12:41.074 --> 00:12:42.701
If that's so, why do you look

00:12:42.743 --> 00:12:45.211
as if you've just signed
my death sentence?

00:12:46.580 --> 00:12:48.207
I'm sorry.

00:12:48.248 --> 00:12:51.547
I guess...
it caught me off guard.

00:12:51.585 --> 00:12:53.553
I wouldn't worry about it.

00:12:53.587 --> 00:12:56.715
Something tells me
that you're going to have

00:12:56.757 --> 00:12:59.749
to put up with me
for a long time to come.

00:12:59.793 --> 00:13:02.626
Well, it won't be
easy, but I'll manage.

00:13:03.663 --> 00:13:04.857
Captain?

00:13:04.898 --> 00:13:07.196
Has Worf found anything?

00:13:07.234 --> 00:13:09.862
No, sir, his security scans
came up negative.

00:13:09.936 --> 00:13:12.200
They're still checking
the sensor logs

00:13:12.239 --> 00:13:15.640
but there is no indication
that you ever left the ship.

00:13:15.675 --> 00:13:16.869
I wasn't dreaming.

00:13:16.943 --> 00:13:18.240
Something happened.

00:13:18.278 --> 00:13:19.336
Worf to Captain.

00:13:19.379 --> 00:13:20.676
Go ahead, Mr. Worf.

00:13:20.714 --> 00:13:23.274
Sir, there is
an incoming transmission

00:13:23.316 --> 00:13:24.544
from Admiral Nakamura.

00:13:24.584 --> 00:13:26.245
It is a priority one message.

00:13:26.286 --> 00:13:27.310
Beverly.

00:13:27.354 --> 00:13:29.845
Mr. Worf,
will you route the call through

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:32.415
to Dr. Crusher's office?

00:13:32.459 --> 00:13:34.450
Aye, sir.

00:13:36.329 --> 00:13:37.796
Captain.

00:13:37.831 --> 00:13:39.128
Admiral.

00:13:39.166 --> 00:13:41.293
I am initiating
a fleet-wide Yellow Alert.

00:13:41.334 --> 00:13:43.268
Starfleet Intelligence
has picked up

00:13:43.303 --> 00:13:45.771
some alarming reports
from the Romulan Empire.

00:13:45.806 --> 00:13:47.137
It appears that at least

00:13:47.174 --> 00:13:49.870
30 warbirds have been pulled
from other assignments

00:13:49.910 --> 00:13:51.775
and are headed
for the Neutral Zone.

00:13:51.812 --> 00:13:54.144
Is there any explanation
why they would make

00:13:54.181 --> 00:13:55.910
such a blatantly
aggressive move?

00:13:55.949 --> 00:13:58.110
Our operatives on Romulus
have indicated

00:13:58.151 --> 00:14:00.517
that there appears
to be something happening

00:14:00.554 --> 00:14:01.543
in the Neutral Zone

00:14:01.588 --> 00:14:03.419
specifically
in the Devron system.

00:14:03.457 --> 00:14:05.618
Our own long-range scans
have picked up

00:14:05.659 --> 00:14:07.957
some kind of spatial anomaly
in the area.

00:14:07.994 --> 00:14:09.427
We can't tell what it is.

00:14:09.463 --> 00:14:10.623
What are our orders?

00:14:10.664 --> 00:14:12.859
This is
a very delicate situation.

00:14:12.966 --> 00:14:15.730
I'm deploying 15 starships
along our side

00:14:15.769 --> 00:14:17.327
of the Neutral Zone.

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:19.804
I want you to go there, as well.

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:22.832
See if you can find out
what is going on

00:14:22.876 --> 00:14:24.537
in the Devron system.

00:14:24.578 --> 00:14:27.274
Hmm. Am I authorized
to enter the Neutral Zone?

00:14:27.314 --> 00:14:28.440
Not yet.

00:14:28.482 --> 00:14:30.575
Wait and see
what the Romulans do.

00:14:30.617 --> 00:14:32.710
You can conduct
long-range scans...

00:14:32.752 --> 00:14:34.379
send probes if necessary...

00:14:34.421 --> 00:14:37.822
but do not cross the border
unless they do.

00:14:37.858 --> 00:14:39.155
Understood.

00:14:39.192 --> 00:14:40.523
Starfleet out.

00:14:45.832 --> 00:14:47.766
Captain.

00:14:49.102 --> 00:14:50.831
What's wrong?

00:14:52.572 --> 00:14:54.733
This is not my time.

00:14:56.710 --> 00:14:58.337
I don't belong here.

00:14:58.378 --> 00:14:59.675
What?

00:14:59.713 --> 00:15:02.147
I was somewhere else
a few moments ago.

00:15:02.182 --> 00:15:03.274
What do you mean?

00:15:03.316 --> 00:15:05.284
You-you've been
right here with me.

00:15:05.318 --> 00:15:07.286
No! No! No!

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:09.311
I was somewhere else.

00:15:09.356 --> 00:15:10.789
I was...

00:15:10.824 --> 00:15:12.655
it was a long time ago.

00:15:12.692 --> 00:15:15.160
There was someone talking.

00:15:15.195 --> 00:15:16.594
I was... I-I...

00:15:16.630 --> 00:15:18.996
I was talking to someone.

00:15:19.032 --> 00:15:20.499
Beverly.

00:15:20.534 --> 00:15:22.229
I was talking to Beverly.

00:15:22.269 --> 00:15:23.497
It's okay, Captain.

00:15:23.537 --> 00:15:25.835
Everything's going
to be all right.

00:15:25.872 --> 00:15:27.669
I'm not senile, you know.

00:15:27.707 --> 00:15:29.004
This did happen.

00:15:29.042 --> 00:15:30.839
I-I-I was here.

00:15:30.877 --> 00:15:33.505
I was talking to you,
and then...

00:15:33.547 --> 00:15:35.515
and then I was somewhere else.

00:15:35.549 --> 00:15:37.676
I was, uh...

00:15:37.717 --> 00:15:39.685
I was on the Enterprise.

00:15:39.719 --> 00:15:41.687
I was back on the Enterprise.

00:15:41.721 --> 00:15:43.279
At least I...

00:15:43.323 --> 00:15:45.188
I think that's where it was.

00:15:45.225 --> 00:15:47.193
I was in Sick Bay.

00:15:47.227 --> 00:15:49.855
I, uh, well, it might
have been a hospital.

00:15:49.896 --> 00:15:52.888
Captain, I think we should
go back to the house

00:15:52.966 --> 00:15:54.331
and call your doctor.

00:15:54.367 --> 00:15:56.494
Yes, yes, I know
what you're thinking.

00:15:56.536 --> 00:15:58.094
It's the Irumodic Syndrome.

00:15:58.138 --> 00:16:00.800
"He's beginning to lose
his mind, the old man."

00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:03.809
Well, it's not that,
and I'm not daydreaming either.

00:16:05.579 --> 00:16:06.807
Well, all right.

00:16:06.846 --> 00:16:08.143
All right.

00:16:08.181 --> 00:16:11.048
So, what do you want
to do about it?

00:16:13.019 --> 00:16:14.145
Data.

00:16:14.187 --> 00:16:16.087
I want to see Data.

00:16:16.122 --> 00:16:17.419
Data... why?

00:16:17.457 --> 00:16:19.152
'Cause I think he can help.

00:16:19.192 --> 00:16:20.489
Help how?

00:16:20.527 --> 00:16:22.825
I don't know!
I don't know!

00:16:22.862 --> 00:16:25.160
I want to see Data.

00:16:25.198 --> 00:16:26.495
Well, okay, then.

00:16:26.533 --> 00:16:28.831
All right, let's...
let's go see Data.

00:16:28.868 --> 00:16:31.666
He's still at Cambridge,
isn't he?

00:16:31.705 --> 00:16:35.471
I... Yes, I-I-I think he is.

00:16:52.325 --> 00:16:54.122
You see them, don't you?

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:56.094
See who?

00:16:56.129 --> 00:16:58.597
They're everywhere.

00:16:58.632 --> 00:17:01.192
They're laughing at me.

00:17:01.234 --> 00:17:02.701
Why are they laughing?

00:17:02.736 --> 00:17:04.397
Come on, Captain.

00:17:04.437 --> 00:17:06.234
Let's go see Data.

00:17:09.009 --> 00:17:10.476
Yes.

00:17:10.510 --> 00:17:12.137
Data.

00:17:12.178 --> 00:17:14.009
We'll go see Data.

00:17:21.554 --> 00:17:24.819
I know how it sounds,
but it happened.

00:17:24.857 --> 00:17:26.324
It was real.

00:17:26.359 --> 00:17:29.328
I was there, back on board
the Enterprise.

00:17:29.362 --> 00:17:31.330
How do you like your tea?

00:17:31.364 --> 00:17:32.991
Tea? Earl Grey. Hot.

00:17:33.032 --> 00:17:34.192
Of course it's hot.

00:17:34.233 --> 00:17:35.666
What do you want in it?

00:17:35.701 --> 00:17:37.168
Nothing.

00:17:37.203 --> 00:17:39.671
Well, Data, I must say

00:17:39.705 --> 00:17:41.866
this is a fine place
you have here.

00:17:41.974 --> 00:17:45.876
They certainly treat professors
very well at Cambridge.

00:17:45.978 --> 00:17:49.277
Holding the Lucasian Chair
does have its perquisites.

00:17:49.315 --> 00:17:51.249
This house originally belonged

00:17:51.284 --> 00:17:53.684
to Sir Isaac Newton
when he held the position.

00:17:53.719 --> 00:17:56.187
It's become
the traditional residence.

00:17:56.222 --> 00:17:57.689
Here you go.

00:17:57.723 --> 00:17:59.156
Thank you.

00:17:59.192 --> 00:18:00.989
If you're really his friend

00:18:01.027 --> 00:18:04.622
you'll get him to take that gray
out of his hair.

00:18:04.664 --> 00:18:05.824
Jessel...

00:18:05.898 --> 00:18:07.832
Looks like a bloody skunk.

00:18:07.867 --> 00:18:09.198
Hmm.

00:18:09.235 --> 00:18:11.669
She can be frightfully trying
at times

00:18:11.704 --> 00:18:14.172
but she does make me laugh.

00:18:16.976 --> 00:18:19.843
Data, what is it
with the hair, anyway?

00:18:19.946 --> 00:18:22.437
Well, I found
that a touch of gray

00:18:22.482 --> 00:18:24.814
adds an air of... distinction.

00:18:24.851 --> 00:18:26.182
You say this is Earl Grey?

00:18:26.219 --> 00:18:27.846
I'd swear
that it was Darjeeling.

00:18:27.887 --> 00:18:29.650
Hmm.

00:18:29.689 --> 00:18:31.554
Captain...

00:18:31.591 --> 00:18:34.822
how long has it been
since you've seen a doctor

00:18:34.861 --> 00:18:37.193
about your Irumodic Syndrome?

00:18:37.230 --> 00:18:39.198
A week.

00:18:39.232 --> 00:18:42.099
They prescribed peridaxon.

00:18:43.402 --> 00:18:45.393
But, sir, peridaxon...

00:18:45.438 --> 00:18:47.030
Yes, I know.
It's not a cure.

00:18:47.073 --> 00:18:49.166
There's nothing that can prevent

00:18:49.208 --> 00:18:51.870
the deterioration
of the synaptic pathways.

00:18:51.978 --> 00:18:53.570
You think that I'm senile

00:18:53.613 --> 00:18:55.706
that all this
is just a delusion.

00:18:55.748 --> 00:18:57.181
Now, come on, Captain.

00:18:57.216 --> 00:18:59.377
No one said anything
of the kind.

00:18:59.418 --> 00:19:01.249
In all honesty, Captain

00:19:01.287 --> 00:19:03.778
the thought has occurred to me.

00:19:04.824 --> 00:19:06.121
However...

00:19:06.158 --> 00:19:08.456
there's nothing to disprove

00:19:08.494 --> 00:19:10.121
what you're saying.

00:19:10.162 --> 00:19:15.828
So it's possible
something is happening to you.

00:19:17.436 --> 00:19:20.371
The first thing we should do
is run a complete series

00:19:20.406 --> 00:19:21.668
of neurographic scans.

00:19:21.707 --> 00:19:24.198
We can use the equipment
in the biometric lab

00:19:24.243 --> 00:19:25.301
here on the campus.

00:19:25.344 --> 00:19:27.141
Jessel, ask Professor Rippert

00:19:27.179 --> 00:19:29.374
to take over my lecture
for tomorrow

00:19:29.415 --> 00:19:30.848
possibly for the rest
of the week.

00:19:30.917 --> 00:19:32.248
Oh, dear...

00:19:32.285 --> 00:19:35.277
Captain, we'll get
to the bottom of this.

00:19:35.321 --> 00:19:37.380
That's the Data that I remember.

00:19:37.423 --> 00:19:39.789
I knew
that I could count on you...

00:19:43.896 --> 00:19:45.989
Commanding Officer

00:19:46.032 --> 00:19:48.296
Enterprise arriving.

00:20:00.546 --> 00:20:04.312
"To Captain Jean-Luc Picard,
Stardate 41148..."

00:20:17.063 --> 00:20:20.555
"...you are hereby requested
and required to take command..."

00:20:26.606 --> 00:20:30.372
"...to take... command
of the USS Enterprise

00:20:30.409 --> 00:20:32.070
as of this date."

00:20:32.111 --> 00:20:35.478
Signed, "Rear Admiral Norah
Satie, Starfleet Command."

00:20:51.564 --> 00:20:52.861
Red Alert!

00:20:52.898 --> 00:20:54.923
All crew to battle stations!

00:20:56.936 --> 00:20:58.164
You heard him.

00:20:58.204 --> 00:20:59.466
Move!

00:21:24.230 --> 00:21:27.461
Personal log, Stardate 41153.7.

00:21:27.500 --> 00:21:31.231
Recorded under security lockout
Omega three-two-seven.

00:21:31.270 --> 00:21:34.603
I have decided not to inform
this crew of my experiences.

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:37.609
If it's true
that I've traveled to the past

00:21:37.643 --> 00:21:40.339
I cannot risk
giving them foreknowledge

00:21:40.379 --> 00:21:42.142
of what's to come.

00:21:49.121 --> 00:21:50.452
Report.

00:21:50.489 --> 00:21:53.583
We've completed
a full subspace scan

00:21:53.626 --> 00:21:55.355
of the ship
and surrounding space.

00:21:55.394 --> 00:21:57.487
We've detected no unusual
readings or anomalies.

00:21:57.530 --> 00:22:00.795
With all due respect, sir,
it would be helpful

00:22:00.833 --> 00:22:03.461
if we knew exactly
what we were looking for.

00:22:03.502 --> 00:22:04.469
Noted.

00:22:04.503 --> 00:22:06.232
Counselor, do you sense

00:22:06.272 --> 00:22:09.207
anything unusual
on board the Enterprise?

00:22:09.241 --> 00:22:12.404
Perhaps an alien presence
that doesn't belong here?

00:22:12.445 --> 00:22:15.346
Maybe one operating
on a level of intelligence

00:22:15.381 --> 00:22:16.643
far superior to our own?

00:22:16.682 --> 00:22:19.810
No, sir, I'm only aware
of the crew and the families

00:22:19.852 --> 00:22:21.752
on board the ship.

00:22:21.787 --> 00:22:25.314
Mr. Worf, initiate
a level-2 security alert...

00:22:25.357 --> 00:22:27.086
all decks...
until further notice.

00:22:27.126 --> 00:22:28.821
With all due respect, sir

00:22:28.861 --> 00:22:31.489
I'm the Security Chief
on this ship.

00:22:31.530 --> 00:22:34.590
Unless... you're planning
to make a change.

00:22:34.633 --> 00:22:37.124
No, uh... of course not.

00:22:37.169 --> 00:22:40.468
Lieutenant, security alert 2.

00:22:40.506 --> 00:22:42.064
Aye, sir.

00:22:42.108 --> 00:22:44.269
Captain Picard to the Bridge,
please.

00:22:44.310 --> 00:22:45.607
We're on our way, Chief.

00:22:50.683 --> 00:22:53.447
Sir, Starfleet just issued
an alert.

00:22:53.486 --> 00:22:54.714
It appears a number of vessels

00:22:54.754 --> 00:22:56.153
are moving
toward the Neutral Zone

00:22:56.188 --> 00:22:57.712
between Romulan
and Federation space.

00:22:57.757 --> 00:22:59.190
What kind of vessels?

00:22:59.225 --> 00:23:00.715
Freighters, transports.

00:23:00.760 --> 00:23:03.661
All civilians...
none of them Starfleet ships.

00:23:03.696 --> 00:23:06.062
This tells me
that a large spatial anomaly

00:23:06.098 --> 00:23:08.658
has appeared
in the Neutral Zone.

00:23:08.701 --> 00:23:10.498
In the Devron system.

00:23:10.536 --> 00:23:12.766
Captain, it could be
a Romulan trick

00:23:12.805 --> 00:23:15.296
to lure our ships
into the Neutral Zone

00:23:15.341 --> 00:23:17.571
as an excuse
for a military strike.

00:23:17.610 --> 00:23:20.078
Starfleet's canceling
our mission to Farpoint Station

00:23:20.112 --> 00:23:21.739
and ordering us
to the Neutral Zone

00:23:21.781 --> 00:23:23.442
as soon as we leave
the spacedock.

00:23:23.482 --> 00:23:25.541
No, we'll proceed to Farpoint.

00:23:25.584 --> 00:23:27.415
Sir?

00:23:27.453 --> 00:23:29.284
You heard me.

00:23:29.321 --> 00:23:31.118
Captain, the security
of the Federation

00:23:31.157 --> 00:23:32.283
could be at stake.

00:23:32.324 --> 00:23:34.417
Mr. Worf, will you man
your station?

00:23:34.460 --> 00:23:36.087
Aye, sir.

00:23:36.128 --> 00:23:37.618
Captain, perhaps
if we understood

00:23:37.663 --> 00:23:39.460
your thinking,
if you could explain...?

00:23:39.498 --> 00:23:41.762
I have no intention
of explaining to anyone.

00:23:41.801 --> 00:23:44.133
We will proceed with our mission
to Farpoint as planned.

00:23:44.170 --> 00:23:45.728
Chief O'Brien,
am I right in thinking

00:23:45.771 --> 00:23:48.331
that you're having a problem
with the warp plasma inducers?

00:23:48.374 --> 00:23:49.636
That's right, sir.

00:23:49.675 --> 00:23:51.404
Well, I know
how to get them back on line.

00:23:51.443 --> 00:23:53.308
You're with me.
We'll be in Main Engineering.

00:24:00.284 --> 00:24:03.219
Mr. O'Brien, will you use
these specifications

00:24:03.254 --> 00:24:05.779
to bypass the secondary
plasma inducer?

00:24:05.823 --> 00:24:07.415
You have to realize, sir

00:24:07.458 --> 00:24:09.426
this isn't exactly
my area of expertise.

00:24:09.460 --> 00:24:10.950
The Chief Engineer

00:24:10.995 --> 00:24:12.758
should be making
these modifications.

00:24:12.796 --> 00:24:15.424
But the Chief Engineer
isn't on board.

00:24:15.466 --> 00:24:17.161
Mr. O'Brien, trust me.

00:24:17.201 --> 00:24:18.828
I know you can do it.

00:24:18.869 --> 00:24:21.235
All those years
you spent as a child

00:24:21.272 --> 00:24:23.706
building those model
starship engines?

00:24:23.741 --> 00:24:25.368
They were well worth it.

00:24:25.409 --> 00:24:27.309
How did you know that, sir?

00:24:27.344 --> 00:24:29.710
From your Starfleet records.

00:24:29.747 --> 00:24:30.805
Oh.

00:24:30.848 --> 00:24:32.213
Yes, sir.

00:24:32.249 --> 00:24:34.240
I'll get right
to these modifications.

00:24:34.285 --> 00:24:37.186
Fletcher, tell Munoz and Lee
to get up here right away.

00:24:37.221 --> 00:24:38.518
Aye, sir.

00:24:38.555 --> 00:24:40.887
We have to realign
the entire power grid.

00:24:40.958 --> 00:24:43.290
We'll all be burning
the midnight oil on this one.

00:24:43.327 --> 00:24:44.453
That would be inadvisable.

00:24:44.495 --> 00:24:45.792
Excuse me?

00:24:45.829 --> 00:24:49.287
If you attempt to ignite
a petroleum product

00:24:49.333 --> 00:24:52.302
on this ship at 00:00 hours,
you will activate

00:24:52.336 --> 00:24:54.099
the fire suppression system

00:24:54.138 --> 00:24:56.868
which would seal off
this entire compartment.

00:24:56.907 --> 00:24:58.841
That was just an expression.

00:24:58.876 --> 00:25:00.309
Expression of what?

00:25:00.344 --> 00:25:01.777
A figure of speech.

00:25:01.812 --> 00:25:05.407
I was trying to tell him
that we'd be working late.

00:25:05.449 --> 00:25:07.679
Ah. Then "to burn
the midnight oil"

00:25:07.718 --> 00:25:08.844
implies late work.

00:25:08.952 --> 00:25:10.852
That's right.

00:25:10.888 --> 00:25:12.253
Hmm. I am curious.

00:25:12.289 --> 00:25:14.985
What is the etymology
of that idiom?

00:25:15.025 --> 00:25:15.992
Hmm?

00:25:16.026 --> 00:25:17.459
How did it come to be used

00:25:17.494 --> 00:25:18.791
in contemporary language?

00:25:18.829 --> 00:25:20.387
Well, I-I don't know, sir.

00:25:20.431 --> 00:25:21.762
Commander Data...

00:25:21.799 --> 00:25:23.664
welcome on board.

00:25:23.701 --> 00:25:25.601
It's so very good to see you.

00:25:25.636 --> 00:25:28.264
It is good to see you, too, sir.

00:25:28.305 --> 00:25:31.763
I could use your help
with the infuser array.

00:25:31.809 --> 00:25:33.470
Certainly.

00:25:37.081 --> 00:25:38.981
As you can see

00:25:39.016 --> 00:25:41.382
we're having problems
with the plasma conduits.

00:25:43.921 --> 00:25:47.584
This will need a completely new
field induction subprocessor.

00:25:47.624 --> 00:25:49.888
It appears we will be required

00:25:49.993 --> 00:25:52.188
to ignite
the midnight petroleum, sir.

00:25:53.230 --> 00:25:55.596
Jean-Luc, what's going on?

00:25:59.770 --> 00:26:01.169
It happened again.

00:26:01.205 --> 00:26:02.570
A time shift?

00:26:02.606 --> 00:26:03.732
Yeah.

00:26:03.774 --> 00:26:05.605
What happened?

00:26:05.642 --> 00:26:08.008
It's still a little vague

00:26:08.045 --> 00:26:11.173
but I can remember
more this time.

00:26:11.215 --> 00:26:14.412
It seems that every time
I shift periods

00:26:14.451 --> 00:26:16.681
I can retain more memory.

00:26:16.720 --> 00:26:19.689
At first, it appeared
that I was in the future...

00:26:19.723 --> 00:26:21.350
years from now...

00:26:21.392 --> 00:26:23.690
and then, I was in the past

00:26:23.727 --> 00:26:26.252
just before our first mission.

00:26:26.296 --> 00:26:27.820
What is it?

00:26:27.865 --> 00:26:31.801
I just scanned his temporal lobe
and compared it with the scan

00:26:31.835 --> 00:26:34.269
I performed
just a few minutes before.

00:26:34.304 --> 00:26:35.737
There's a 13% increase

00:26:35.773 --> 00:26:38.298
in the acetylcholine
of the hippocampus.

00:26:38.342 --> 00:26:41.368
Within a matter of minutes,
you have accumulated

00:26:41.412 --> 00:26:43.471
over two days' worth
of memories.

00:26:51.989 --> 00:26:53.149
Counselor, do you remember

00:26:53.190 --> 00:26:55.181
when I first came
on board the Enterprise?

00:26:55.225 --> 00:26:56.385
Yes.

00:26:56.427 --> 00:26:59.055
What happened
after the welcoming ceremony?

00:26:59.096 --> 00:27:01.030
There was a reception
in Ten-Forward.

00:27:01.064 --> 00:27:04.090
I introduced you to Worf
and the other senior officers.

00:27:04.134 --> 00:27:06.762
Do you have any memory
of my calling Red Alert

00:27:06.804 --> 00:27:07.828
in the spacedock?

00:27:07.938 --> 00:27:09.997
Do you remember Starfleet
diverting us

00:27:10.040 --> 00:27:11.803
from Farpoint
to the Neutral Zone

00:27:11.842 --> 00:27:13.639
to investigate
a spatial anomaly?

00:27:13.677 --> 00:27:15.201
No.

00:27:15.245 --> 00:27:18.043
It would appear
there is a discontinuity

00:27:18.081 --> 00:27:19.844
between the time periods
you described.

00:27:19.950 --> 00:27:21.110
Events in one time period

00:27:21.151 --> 00:27:23.051
would seem to have
no effect on the other two.

00:27:23.086 --> 00:27:24.576
Yet, in both the past
and the present

00:27:24.621 --> 00:27:27.181
there was a report of the same
anomaly in the Devron system.

00:27:27.224 --> 00:27:29.522
I find it hard to believe
that that's a coincidence.

00:27:29.560 --> 00:27:32.324
For all I know, I may find
the same thing in the future.

00:27:32.362 --> 00:27:33.522
Perhaps the anomaly is

00:27:33.564 --> 00:27:35.498
a temporal disturbance
of some kind.

00:27:35.532 --> 00:27:38.467
How is all this related
to your time shifting?

00:27:38.502 --> 00:27:40.493
These are all
very important questions

00:27:40.537 --> 00:27:43.267
and perhaps I will find
answers to them in the past.

00:27:43.307 --> 00:27:45.832
But now, we have
a potentially dangerous threat

00:27:45.876 --> 00:27:46.865
from the Romulans.

00:27:46.910 --> 00:27:49.037
I want all departments
to present

00:27:49.079 --> 00:27:51.411
a battle readiness report
to me at 0800 hours

00:27:51.448 --> 00:27:53.746
tomorrow morning.
Dismissed.

00:27:53.784 --> 00:27:56.753
Deanna, it's going to be
a late night.

00:27:56.787 --> 00:27:58.982
Would you like to have
some dinner first?

00:27:59.022 --> 00:28:00.819
Actually, I...

00:28:02.793 --> 00:28:04.454
We have plans.

00:28:04.495 --> 00:28:06.156
Oh, I see.
I'm sorry.

00:28:06.196 --> 00:28:08.460
I'll see you in the morning.

00:28:11.668 --> 00:28:13.067
Good night, sir.

00:28:13.103 --> 00:28:15.128
Worf.

00:28:19.009 --> 00:28:21.034
I want continual
subspace sweeps.

00:28:21.078 --> 00:28:24.104
We may be able to detect
a temporal disturbance.

00:28:24.147 --> 00:28:25.409
Aye, sir.

00:28:25.449 --> 00:28:28.282
Will... this time shifting...

00:28:28.318 --> 00:28:31.617
when it happens, I experience
a momentary disorientation.

00:28:31.655 --> 00:28:34.715
If that should happen
during a crisis, Will

00:28:34.758 --> 00:28:38.125
I want you
to take command immediately.

00:28:38.161 --> 00:28:39.560
Number One?

00:28:39.596 --> 00:28:41.223
I'm sorry.

00:28:41.265 --> 00:28:43.859
Be prepared to take command.
Aye, sir.

00:28:43.934 --> 00:28:46.425
Speaking of disorientation,
are you all right?

00:28:46.470 --> 00:28:48.768
I'm just a little distracted.
I'm fine.

00:28:51.808 --> 00:28:53.708
You have the Bridge, Number One.

00:28:53.744 --> 00:28:55.939
I'II... I'll be
in my ready room.

00:29:04.021 --> 00:29:05.420
Come.

00:29:10.894 --> 00:29:12.589
Milk, warm.

00:29:12.629 --> 00:29:14.096
A dash of nutmeg.

00:29:14.131 --> 00:29:15.792
What's this?

00:29:17.134 --> 00:29:18.624
A prescription.

00:29:18.669 --> 00:29:20.637
A glass of warm milk

00:29:20.671 --> 00:29:22.832
and eight hours'
uninterrupted sleep.

00:29:22.873 --> 00:29:24.738
Beverly...?

00:29:24.775 --> 00:29:26.936
Doctor's orders.

00:29:26.977 --> 00:29:28.342
You're exhausted.

00:29:28.378 --> 00:29:30.642
Look, I don't know
whether you slept

00:29:30.681 --> 00:29:32.444
in the past or in the future

00:29:32.482 --> 00:29:35.451
but I'm sure you haven't
slept in the present.

00:29:35.485 --> 00:29:38.386
Now, get some rest,
or I'll have you relieved

00:29:38.422 --> 00:29:39.855
and sedated.

00:29:39.923 --> 00:29:41.550
Yes, sir.

00:29:45.362 --> 00:29:47.159
What?

00:29:48.565 --> 00:29:50.089
Hey.

00:29:51.835 --> 00:29:53.632
Beverly?

00:29:57.007 --> 00:29:59.168
As a physician,
it's often my job

00:29:59.209 --> 00:30:01.302
to give people unpleasant news...

00:30:01.345 --> 00:30:03.677
to tell them
that they need surgery

00:30:03.714 --> 00:30:06.842
or that they can't have children

00:30:06.883 --> 00:30:10.319
or that they might be facing
a difficult illness.

00:30:10.354 --> 00:30:13.755
But you said yourself
that this is only a possibility.

00:30:15.759 --> 00:30:17.784
But you've been to the future.

00:30:17.828 --> 00:30:20.194
You know it's going to happen.

00:30:20.230 --> 00:30:22.494
I prefer to look on the future

00:30:22.532 --> 00:30:25.990
as something
which is not written in stone.

00:30:27.904 --> 00:30:31.340
A lot of things can happen
in 25 years.

00:30:45.622 --> 00:30:48.420
A lot of things can happen.

00:30:56.400 --> 00:30:57.934
Captain?

00:30:58.067 --> 00:31:00.695
Yeah?

00:31:00.736 --> 00:31:02.135
Captain, wake up.

00:31:02.171 --> 00:31:04.230
Yes.

00:31:06.175 --> 00:31:07.608
What is it?

00:31:07.643 --> 00:31:10.203
Have we reached
the Neutral Zone?

00:31:10.246 --> 00:31:12.578
The Neutral Zone?

00:31:15.151 --> 00:31:17.085
Oh...

00:31:17.119 --> 00:31:19.087
I'm sorry.

00:31:19.121 --> 00:31:21.385
I was in the past again.

00:31:21.424 --> 00:31:23.051
What's going on?

00:31:23.092 --> 00:31:25.583
Data's arranged for us
to run those tests on you

00:31:25.628 --> 00:31:26.822
in the biometrics lab.

00:31:26.862 --> 00:31:28.420
We're ready to go, if you are.

00:31:28.464 --> 00:31:30.489
No, no, no, no.

00:31:30.533 --> 00:31:33.001
We have to get
to the Neutral Zone.

00:31:33.035 --> 00:31:35.697
The Neutral Zone? Why?

00:31:35.738 --> 00:31:38.263
In the other two time periods

00:31:38.307 --> 00:31:41.902
Starfleet reported... a...

00:31:41.944 --> 00:31:44.105
a-a-a sort of a...

00:31:44.146 --> 00:31:48.310
a spatial anomaly in-in-in...

00:31:48.351 --> 00:31:50.114
in the Devron system.

00:31:50.152 --> 00:31:53.713
In the Devron system
in the Neutral Zone.

00:31:53.756 --> 00:31:55.121
Captain...?

00:31:55.157 --> 00:31:57.557
I-I-lf the anomaly
appeared there in the past

00:31:57.593 --> 00:32:00.323
then it might be here, too,
and we have to find out.

00:32:00.363 --> 00:32:02.831
Just because you've seen it
in two other time frames

00:32:02.865 --> 00:32:04.833
doesn't mean that
it's going to be here.

00:32:04.867 --> 00:32:08.132
Yeah, but if it is here,
then it means something!

00:32:08.170 --> 00:32:09.159
Damn it, Geordi!

00:32:09.205 --> 00:32:11.298
I-I know what we have to do!

00:32:15.177 --> 00:32:16.508
All right.

00:32:17.680 --> 00:32:21.741
Okay, but first,
there is no Neutral Zone.

00:32:21.784 --> 00:32:23.149
Remember?

00:32:23.185 --> 00:32:24.709
Right.

00:32:24.754 --> 00:32:27.484
Right. Klingons.

00:32:27.523 --> 00:32:29.491
In this time period

00:32:29.525 --> 00:32:32.153
the Klingons have taken over
the Romulan Empire.

00:32:32.194 --> 00:32:34.094
And right now,
relations between us

00:32:34.130 --> 00:32:36.098
and the Klingons
aren't too cozy.

00:32:36.132 --> 00:32:37.463
I know that!

00:32:37.500 --> 00:32:39.934
I haven't completely lost
my mind, you know.

00:32:42.505 --> 00:32:46.703
Well... if we're going
to the Devron system

00:32:46.742 --> 00:32:49.575
we're going to need a ship.

00:32:52.715 --> 00:32:54.307
Right.

00:32:54.350 --> 00:32:56.614
Now...

00:32:56.652 --> 00:33:01.715
I think it's time
to call in some old favors.

00:33:01.757 --> 00:33:03.418
Contact...

00:33:03.459 --> 00:33:07.452
Admiral Riker, Starbase 247.

00:33:13.169 --> 00:33:15.330
Jean-Luc, you know
I'd like to help

00:33:15.371 --> 00:33:17.965
but frankly, what you're asking
for is impossible.

00:33:18.007 --> 00:33:20.202
The Klingons have closed
their borders

00:33:20.242 --> 00:33:21.869
to all Federation starships.

00:33:21.911 --> 00:33:23.845
Will,
what if this spatial anomaly

00:33:23.879 --> 00:33:25.744
really is
in the Devron system?

00:33:25.781 --> 00:33:28.614
I saw a report
from Starfleet Intelligence

00:33:28.651 --> 00:33:30.585
this morning on that sector.

00:33:30.619 --> 00:33:32.280
There is no activity.

00:33:32.321 --> 00:33:35.882
There is nothing unusual
going on in the Devron system.

00:33:35.958 --> 00:33:37.391
Well, I don't believe it.

00:33:37.426 --> 00:33:39.792
What if their
long-range scans are faulty?

00:33:39.829 --> 00:33:42.297
We have to go there
and see for ourselves.

00:33:42.331 --> 00:33:44.993
Look, I've got the Yorktown
out near the border.

00:33:45.034 --> 00:33:47.195
I'll have her run
some long-range scans

00:33:47.236 --> 00:33:48.498
in the Devron system.

00:33:48.537 --> 00:33:50.801
If she finds out anything,
I'll let you know.

00:33:50.840 --> 00:33:52.671
Will, that is just not
good enough.

00:33:52.708 --> 00:33:54.539
It's going to have to be.
I'm sorry.

00:33:54.577 --> 00:33:56.306
It's all I can do.
Riker out.

00:34:00.483 --> 00:34:02.713
Computer, restore
holographic image.

00:34:04.954 --> 00:34:06.854
Damn him, anyway.

00:34:06.956 --> 00:34:09.254
After all we've
been through together.

00:34:09.291 --> 00:34:12.954
He's been sitting
behind that desk too long.

00:34:12.995 --> 00:34:14.587
Captain, I'm sorry.

00:34:14.630 --> 00:34:18.031
I guess all we can do
now is wait and see

00:34:18.067 --> 00:34:20.365
if the Yorktown finds anything.

00:34:20.402 --> 00:34:22.233
There is another option.

00:34:22.271 --> 00:34:25.729
We could arrange passage
aboard a medical ship.

00:34:25.774 --> 00:34:27.571
Medical ship?

00:34:27.610 --> 00:34:30.477
Yes, sir. There was an outbreak
of Terrellian plague on Romulus.

00:34:30.513 --> 00:34:31.878
The Klingons have been allowing

00:34:31.947 --> 00:34:33.972
Federation medical ships
to cross the border.

00:34:34.016 --> 00:34:36.814
Yes! Yes!

00:34:36.852 --> 00:34:41.186
So, what we need now
is a medical ship.

00:34:41.223 --> 00:34:43.885
I think I can arrange that.

00:34:43.993 --> 00:34:46.223
Data, find the USS Pasteur.

00:34:46.262 --> 00:34:48.321
I...

00:34:48.364 --> 00:34:52.994
I have some pull
with the Captain.

00:34:53.035 --> 00:34:56.527
At least, I used to have.

00:35:12.021 --> 00:35:13.579
Well, this is a page
from the past.

00:35:13.622 --> 00:35:15.613
I never thought
I'd see either of you

00:35:15.658 --> 00:35:16.852
on a starship again.

00:35:16.959 --> 00:35:17.857
Hello, Doctor.

00:35:17.960 --> 00:35:18.858
Geordi.

00:35:18.961 --> 00:35:19.859
Doctor.

00:35:19.962 --> 00:35:20.951
Data.

00:35:22.198 --> 00:35:23.358
Uh...

00:35:25.801 --> 00:35:27.029
Let's just choose one.

00:35:27.069 --> 00:35:28.036
All right...

00:35:28.070 --> 00:35:30.732
Oh.

00:35:30.773 --> 00:35:33.537
So, did you get my message?

00:35:33.576 --> 00:35:36.841
Yes. Jean-Luc, crossing
into Klingon territory...

00:35:36.879 --> 00:35:38.141
it's absurd.

00:35:38.180 --> 00:35:40.114
But then, I never
could say no to you.

00:35:40.149 --> 00:35:42.242
Oh, so that's why
you married me.

00:35:45.221 --> 00:35:48.156
Well, now,
the first order of business

00:35:48.190 --> 00:35:49.714
is to get clearance

00:35:49.758 --> 00:35:51.817
to cross the Klingon border.

00:35:51.860 --> 00:35:52.827
Agreed.

00:35:52.861 --> 00:35:53.828
What about Worf?

00:35:53.862 --> 00:35:55.830
Yes! That's it! Worf.

00:35:55.864 --> 00:35:57.889
Yes, that's the answer.

00:35:58.000 --> 00:35:59.661
Worf will help us.

00:35:59.702 --> 00:36:02.796
Data, isn't Worf still a member
of the Klingon High Council?

00:36:02.838 --> 00:36:04.169
I'm not sure.

00:36:04.206 --> 00:36:07.232
Information on the Klingon
political structure

00:36:07.276 --> 00:36:09.301
is hard to come by these days.

00:36:09.345 --> 00:36:12.940
However, at last report,
Worf was Governor of H'atoria

00:36:12.982 --> 00:36:15.007
a small Klingon colony
near the border.

00:36:15.050 --> 00:36:16.312
Captain Picard?

00:36:16.352 --> 00:36:17.319
- Yes?
- Yes?

00:36:17.353 --> 00:36:19.412
Captain, McKinley
Station is signaling.

00:36:19.455 --> 00:36:21.582
They want to know
when we'll be docking.

00:36:21.624 --> 00:36:23.285
Tell McKinley
we've been called away

00:36:23.325 --> 00:36:24.383
on a priority mission.

00:36:24.426 --> 00:36:25.688
Aye, sir.

00:36:25.728 --> 00:36:27.457
So, you kept the name.

00:36:27.496 --> 00:36:30.124
I've prepared quarters
for you on deck five.

00:36:30.165 --> 00:36:31.792
You might want to get some rest.

00:36:31.834 --> 00:36:33.267
No, I'm fine.
I don't need rest.

00:36:33.302 --> 00:36:36.362
Nell, please escort
the Ambassador to his quarters.

00:36:36.405 --> 00:36:38.771
Look, you are treating me
as if I am an invalid.

00:36:38.807 --> 00:36:41.241
I do have a few years
left in me yet.

00:36:41.277 --> 00:36:43.302
I do not want to be led around

00:36:43.345 --> 00:36:46.439
and I do not want
to be patronized.

00:36:46.482 --> 00:36:48.109
You're right.

00:36:48.150 --> 00:36:49.811
I'm sorry.

00:36:49.852 --> 00:36:51.581
Now, I'll go and get some rest.

00:36:59.862 --> 00:37:03.093
How long since
his last neurological scan?

00:37:03.132 --> 00:37:04.429
I'm not sure

00:37:04.466 --> 00:37:06.366
but I wouldn't try
suggesting it.

00:37:06.402 --> 00:37:08.962
He says he's not taking
any more damn tests.

00:37:09.004 --> 00:37:13.407
Do you really think
he's moving through time?

00:37:20.449 --> 00:37:22.349
I'm not sure I do, either.

00:37:22.384 --> 00:37:25.649
But he's Jean-Luc Picard

00:37:25.688 --> 00:37:27.246
and if he wants to go
on one more mission

00:37:27.289 --> 00:37:29.757
that's what we're going to do.

00:37:31.260 --> 00:37:33.160
We'll find the anomaly.

00:37:34.863 --> 00:37:36.922
I know we will.

00:37:39.568 --> 00:37:41.001
Report.

00:37:41.036 --> 00:37:44.699
We're nearing the coordinates
you gave me, sir.

00:37:44.740 --> 00:37:47.868
Is there anything unusual
in the vicinity, Mr. Data?

00:37:47.910 --> 00:37:50.071
How would you define
"unusual," sir?

00:37:50.112 --> 00:37:53.206
Every region of space
has its own unique properties

00:37:53.248 --> 00:37:55.341
that cannot be found
anywhere else.

00:37:55.384 --> 00:37:59.377
There should be
a barrier of some sort nearby...

00:37:59.421 --> 00:38:01.082
a large plasma field

00:38:01.123 --> 00:38:02.420
highly disruptive.

00:38:02.458 --> 00:38:03.755
Nothing, sir.

00:38:05.828 --> 00:38:09.389
This is the right time,
the right place.

00:38:10.799 --> 00:38:12.824
He should be here now.

00:38:12.868 --> 00:38:15.496
Who, sir?

00:38:15.537 --> 00:38:19.439
Q! We're here.

00:38:19.475 --> 00:38:22.035
This has gone on long enough.

00:38:26.048 --> 00:38:28.846
Counselor, do you sense
an alien presence?

00:38:28.951 --> 00:38:30.851
No, sir.

00:38:34.656 --> 00:38:37.147
What is a "Q?"

00:38:37.192 --> 00:38:40.719
It's a letter of the alphabet
as far as I know.

00:38:40.763 --> 00:38:42.788
I don't understand.

00:38:42.831 --> 00:38:46.130
This is not the way
it's supposed to happen.

00:38:46.168 --> 00:38:47.465
Maintain this position.

00:38:47.503 --> 00:38:49.528
I'll be in my ready room.

00:39:19.001 --> 00:39:21.196
Mon Capitain.

00:39:21.236 --> 00:39:23.261
I thought you'd never get here.

00:39:30.211 --> 00:39:31.439
Q, I knew it.

00:39:31.479 --> 00:39:33.037
What's going on?

00:39:33.081 --> 00:39:34.742
It's "Judge Q" to you.

00:39:34.782 --> 00:39:37.808
And isn't it obvious
what's going on?

00:39:39.754 --> 00:39:43.815
The last time that I stood here
was seven years ago.

00:39:43.858 --> 00:39:45.155
Seven years ago?

00:39:45.193 --> 00:39:47.559
How little do you mortals
understand time.

00:39:47.595 --> 00:39:49.620
Must you be so linear, Jean-Luc?

00:39:49.664 --> 00:39:52.827
You accused me
of being the representative

00:39:52.867 --> 00:39:55.062
of a... a barbarous species.

00:39:55.103 --> 00:39:57.469
I believe my exact words were

00:39:57.505 --> 00:40:00.269
"a dangerous,
savage, child-race."

00:40:04.479 --> 00:40:05.878
We demonstrated to you

00:40:05.947 --> 00:40:09.075
that mankind had become
peaceful and benevolent.

00:40:09.117 --> 00:40:11.278
You agreed,
and you let us go on our way.

00:40:11.319 --> 00:40:13.480
Now, why am I standing
here again?

00:40:13.521 --> 00:40:15.614
Oh, you'd like me
to connect the dots for you...

00:40:15.657 --> 00:40:17.591
lead you from "a" to "b" to "c"

00:40:17.625 --> 00:40:21.652
so that your puny mind
could comprehend.

00:40:21.696 --> 00:40:24.529
How boring.

00:40:28.169 --> 00:40:30.399
They'd be so much
more entertained

00:40:30.438 --> 00:40:32.531
if you just tried
to figure it out.

00:40:32.573 --> 00:40:36.703
I'll answer any ten questions

00:40:36.744 --> 00:40:40.475
that call for a "yes" or a "no."

00:40:42.483 --> 00:40:44.542
Well?

00:40:44.585 --> 00:40:47.748
Are you putting mankind
on trial again?

00:40:47.789 --> 00:40:49.552
No.

00:40:52.126 --> 00:40:53.889
Is there any connection

00:40:53.928 --> 00:40:56.396
between the trial
seven years ago

00:40:56.431 --> 00:40:58.399
and what's happening now?

00:40:58.433 --> 00:41:01.095
I'd have to say yes.

00:41:04.105 --> 00:41:08.542
The spatial anomaly
in the Neutral Zone...

00:41:08.576 --> 00:41:12.137
is it related
to what's going on?

00:41:12.180 --> 00:41:14.341
Most definitely yes.

00:41:14.382 --> 00:41:18.318
Is it part of a Romulan plot...
a ploy to start a war?

00:41:18.353 --> 00:41:20.344
No and no.

00:41:23.825 --> 00:41:25.486
Five down!

00:41:25.526 --> 00:41:26.550
That's only four.

00:41:26.594 --> 00:41:28.289
Is it a Romulan plot?

00:41:28.329 --> 00:41:30.661
Is it a ploy to start a war?

00:41:30.698 --> 00:41:33.599
Those are separate questions.

00:41:35.303 --> 00:41:37.328
Did you create the anomaly?

00:41:37.372 --> 00:41:38.771
No, no, no.

00:41:38.806 --> 00:41:41.036
You're going to be so surprised

00:41:41.075 --> 00:41:43.737
when you realize
where it came from...

00:41:43.778 --> 00:41:45.678
if you ever figure it out.

00:41:45.713 --> 00:41:48.773
Are you responsible
for my shifting through time?

00:41:48.816 --> 00:41:51.307
I'll answer that question

00:41:51.352 --> 00:41:54.879
if you promise
you won't tell anyone.

00:41:56.824 --> 00:41:57.791
Yes.

00:41:57.825 --> 00:41:58.792
Why?

00:41:58.826 --> 00:41:59.918
Sorry!

00:42:00.028 --> 00:42:01.825
That's not a "yes"
or "no" question.

00:42:01.863 --> 00:42:03.797
You forfeit the rest
of your questions.

00:42:07.435 --> 00:42:08.800
Oh, I expected as much.

00:42:08.836 --> 00:42:11.066
You're such
a limited creature...

00:42:11.105 --> 00:42:14.268
a perfect example
of why we made our decision.

00:42:14.308 --> 00:42:17.436
The trial never ended, Captain.

00:42:17.478 --> 00:42:20.242
We never reached a verdict.

00:42:20.281 --> 00:42:21.680
But now we have.

00:42:21.716 --> 00:42:23.013
You're guilty.

00:42:23.051 --> 00:42:24.348
Guilty of what?

00:42:24.385 --> 00:42:25.682
Of being inferior.

00:42:25.720 --> 00:42:28.883
Seven years ago,
I said we'd be watching you

00:42:28.923 --> 00:42:30.220
and we have been.

00:42:30.258 --> 00:42:32.488
Hoping that your ape-like race

00:42:32.527 --> 00:42:36.156
would demonstrate some growth,
give some indication

00:42:36.197 --> 00:42:38.995
that your minds
had room for expansion.

00:42:39.033 --> 00:42:41.263
But what have we seen, instead?

00:42:41.302 --> 00:42:44.430
You worrying about
Commander Riker's career...

00:42:44.472 --> 00:42:48.238
listening to Counselor Troi's
pedantic psycho-babble...

00:42:48.276 --> 00:42:53.908
indulging Data in his witless
exploration of humanity.

00:42:54.015 --> 00:42:55.915
We've journeyed
to countless new worlds.

00:42:55.983 --> 00:42:57.610
We've contacted new species.

00:42:57.652 --> 00:42:58.914
We have expanded

00:42:58.953 --> 00:43:01.046
our understanding
of the universe.

00:43:01.089 --> 00:43:03.057
In your own paltry, limited way.

00:43:03.091 --> 00:43:06.060
You have no idea
how far you still have to go.

00:43:06.094 --> 00:43:08.858
But instead of using
the last seven years

00:43:08.896 --> 00:43:12.798
to change and to grow,
you have squandered them.

00:43:12.834 --> 00:43:16.600
We are what we are,
and we're doing the best we can.

00:43:16.637 --> 00:43:19.401
It is not for you
to set the standards

00:43:19.440 --> 00:43:21.237
by which we should be judged.

00:43:21.275 --> 00:43:23.004
Oh, but it is, and we have.

00:43:23.044 --> 00:43:26.502
Time may be eternal, Captain,
but our patience is not.

00:43:26.547 --> 00:43:30.005
It's time to put an end
to your trek through the stars

00:43:30.051 --> 00:43:33.418
make room for other
more worthy species.

00:43:33.454 --> 00:43:37.322
You're going to deny us
travel through space?

00:43:37.358 --> 00:43:38.586
No...

00:43:40.628 --> 00:43:42.619
You obtuse piece of flotsam.

00:43:42.663 --> 00:43:44.824
You're to be denied existence.

00:43:44.866 --> 00:43:47.164
Humanity's fate has been sealed.

00:43:47.201 --> 00:43:48.725
You will be destroyed.

00:43:48.769 --> 00:43:49.895
Q, I do not believe

00:43:49.971 --> 00:43:52.633
that even you
are capable of such an act.

00:43:52.673 --> 00:43:53.901
"L"?
There you go again...

00:43:54.008 --> 00:43:55.908
always blaming me
for everything.

00:43:55.943 --> 00:43:58.104
Well, this time,
I'm not your enemy.

00:43:58.146 --> 00:44:01.513
I'm not the one that causes
the annihilation of mankind.

00:44:01.549 --> 00:44:02.743
You are.

00:44:02.783 --> 00:44:03.807
Me?

00:44:03.851 --> 00:44:05.182
That's right.

00:44:05.219 --> 00:44:07.119
You're doing it right now.

00:44:07.155 --> 00:44:10.488
You did it before,
and you'll do it yet again.

00:44:10.525 --> 00:44:13.016
What sort of meaningless
double-talk is this?

00:44:13.060 --> 00:44:15.085
He doesn't understand.

00:44:15.129 --> 00:44:19.793
I have only myself to blame,
I suppose.

00:44:19.834 --> 00:44:21.062
I believed in you.

00:44:21.102 --> 00:44:22.865
I thought you had potential

00:44:22.970 --> 00:44:25.302
but, apparently, I was wrong.

00:44:25.339 --> 00:44:28.740
May whatever god
you believe in...

00:44:28.776 --> 00:44:31.040
have mercy on your soul.

00:44:31.078 --> 00:44:33.808
This court stands adjourned.

00:44:45.960 --> 00:44:47.985
Commander, assemble
the senior staff

00:44:48.029 --> 00:44:49.496
and go to Red Alert.

00:44:49.530 --> 00:44:51.725
We have a bigger problem
than I thought.

00:44:51.766 --> 00:44:53.631
Red Alert!

00:45:04.845 --> 00:45:06.005
I don't believe him.

00:45:06.047 --> 00:45:08.038
This has to be another one
of Q's games.

00:45:08.082 --> 00:45:09.947
He's probably listening
to us right now

00:45:09.984 --> 00:45:11.110
getting a big laugh

00:45:11.152 --> 00:45:12.847
out of watching us
jump through his hoops.

00:45:12.954 --> 00:45:14.683
And normally, I would
agree with you

00:45:14.722 --> 00:45:17.350
but this time I feel
that somehow it is different.

00:45:17.391 --> 00:45:20.053
There was a deadly earnestness
about him.

00:45:20.094 --> 00:45:21.823
I think he's serious...

00:45:21.862 --> 00:45:24.490
which means that,
in some fashion

00:45:24.532 --> 00:45:27.865
I am going to be the cause
of the destruction of humanity.

00:45:27.902 --> 00:45:30.393
But didn't Q say
you already had caused it?

00:45:30.438 --> 00:45:33.464
And that you
were causing it now?

00:45:33.507 --> 00:45:36.408
Given the fact that there
is an apparent discontinuity

00:45:36.444 --> 00:45:39.413
between the three time periods
the Captain has visited

00:45:39.447 --> 00:45:41.711
Q's statement may be accurate,
if confusing.

00:45:41.749 --> 00:45:43.444
So, what am I going to do?

00:45:43.484 --> 00:45:44.883
Lock myself in a room

00:45:44.919 --> 00:45:47.046
in all the three
different time periods?

00:45:47.088 --> 00:45:48.817
Captain, maybe not
acting is what causes

00:45:48.856 --> 00:45:50.016
the destruction of mankind.

00:45:50.057 --> 00:45:51.649
What if you were needed
on the Bridge

00:45:51.692 --> 00:45:53.353
and at a key moment,
you weren't there?

00:45:53.394 --> 00:45:55.988
I don't think we can start
second-guessing ourselves.

00:45:56.030 --> 00:45:57.622
I think we have
to proceed normally

00:45:57.665 --> 00:46:00.225
and deal with each situation
as it occurs.

00:46:00.268 --> 00:46:01.326
Agreed.

00:46:01.369 --> 00:46:03.667
I've been thinking
about my conversation with Q.

00:46:03.704 --> 00:46:06.002
He admitted
that he was responsible

00:46:06.040 --> 00:46:07.837
for my shifting through time.

00:46:07.908 --> 00:46:10.468
Now, it occurred to me that...

00:46:10.511 --> 00:46:15.278
he might be giving me a chance
somehow to save humanity.

00:46:15.316 --> 00:46:16.715
What makes you say that?

00:46:16.751 --> 00:46:17.718
Well, he's always had

00:46:17.752 --> 00:46:19.379
a certain fascination
with humanity

00:46:19.420 --> 00:46:20.682
with myself, in particular.

00:46:20.721 --> 00:46:22.689
I think he has more
than a passing interest

00:46:22.723 --> 00:46:24.020
in what happens to me.

00:46:24.058 --> 00:46:25.116
That is true.

00:46:25.159 --> 00:46:27.423
Q's interest in you
has always been

00:46:27.461 --> 00:46:29.520
very similar to that of a master

00:46:29.563 --> 00:46:31.121
and his beloved pet.

00:46:31.165 --> 00:46:33.656
That was only an analogy,
Captain.

00:46:33.701 --> 00:46:34.998
Captain Picard?

00:46:35.036 --> 00:46:36.560
Go ahead.

00:46:36.604 --> 00:46:39.198
We're approaching
the Neutral Zone, Captain.

00:46:39.240 --> 00:46:40.798
We're on our way.

00:46:42.877 --> 00:46:44.071
All stop.

00:46:44.111 --> 00:46:46.443
Initiate long-range scans.

00:46:52.453 --> 00:46:55.684
Captain, there are four warbirds
holding position

00:46:55.723 --> 00:46:58.351
on the Romulan side
of the Neutral Zone.

00:46:58.392 --> 00:47:00.451
The Federation starships
Concord and Bozeman

00:47:00.494 --> 00:47:02.792
are holding position
on our side.

00:47:02.830 --> 00:47:04.127
A face-off.

00:47:04.165 --> 00:47:06.929
The question is,
who's going to move first?

00:47:06.967 --> 00:47:08.195
We are.

00:47:08.235 --> 00:47:11.033
Mr. Worf,
hail the Romulan flagship.

00:47:11.072 --> 00:47:15.236
The Warbird Terix is responding.

00:47:15.276 --> 00:47:17.210
Captain Picard.

00:47:17.244 --> 00:47:18.541
Hello, Worf.

00:47:18.579 --> 00:47:21.571
It's been a long time.

00:47:21.615 --> 00:47:23.378
It is good to see you again.

00:47:23.417 --> 00:47:27.288
Have you had a chance
to read our request?

00:47:27.421 --> 00:47:28.854
Yes, but you must realize

00:47:28.889 --> 00:47:31.687
I am no longer a member
of the High Council.

00:47:31.725 --> 00:47:34.558
But surely, Worf, you must
still have some influence.

00:47:34.595 --> 00:47:36.495
We have to get
into the Neutral Zone.

00:47:36.530 --> 00:47:39.624
Can't you just get us permission
to cross the border?

00:47:39.667 --> 00:47:40.861
I must refuse.

00:47:40.968 --> 00:47:43.061
It is for your own safety.

00:47:43.103 --> 00:47:46.402
The Neutral Zone
is extremely volatile.

00:47:46.440 --> 00:47:50.467
If Admiral Riker had given you
a starship with a cloak

00:47:50.511 --> 00:47:52.240
you would have been safe.

00:47:52.279 --> 00:47:53.871
It is hard to believe

00:47:53.947 --> 00:47:56.211
that even he would refuse
to help you.

00:47:56.250 --> 00:47:59.242
I don't care
what kind of ship we go in!

00:47:59.286 --> 00:48:02.016
We have to get
to the Devron system.

00:48:02.056 --> 00:48:03.353
I am sorry.

00:48:03.390 --> 00:48:06.188
My first duty is to the Empire.

00:48:06.226 --> 00:48:08.353
I must adhere to regulations.

00:48:08.395 --> 00:48:10.795
Well, I know
that I am an old man

00:48:10.831 --> 00:48:12.355
and I'm out of touch

00:48:12.399 --> 00:48:16.802
but the Worf that I remember
was more concerned with things

00:48:16.837 --> 00:48:18.566
like honor and Ioyalty

00:48:18.605 --> 00:48:21.335
than rules and regulations.

00:48:21.375 --> 00:48:24.538
But that was a long time ago.

00:48:24.578 --> 00:48:28.674
And maybe you're not
the Worf I once knew.

00:48:28.716 --> 00:48:29.978
Dor-sHo GHA!

00:48:30.017 --> 00:48:32.952
You have always used

00:48:32.986 --> 00:48:34.954
your knowledge
of Klingon honor and tradition

00:48:34.988 --> 00:48:37.252
to get what you want from me.

00:48:37.291 --> 00:48:39.657
Because it always works, Worf!

00:48:39.693 --> 00:48:40.990
Your problem is

00:48:41.028 --> 00:48:43.326
that you really do
have a sense of honor

00:48:43.364 --> 00:48:46.458
and you really do care
about trust and Ioyalty.

00:48:46.500 --> 00:48:49.663
Don't blame me
for knowing you so well.

00:48:49.703 --> 00:48:51.136
Very well.

00:48:51.171 --> 00:48:54.140
You may cross the border.

00:48:54.174 --> 00:48:55.971
But...

00:48:56.009 --> 00:48:58.443
only if I come with you.

00:48:58.479 --> 00:49:01.778
I am familiar
with the Neutral Zone.

00:49:04.585 --> 00:49:06.610
Terms accepted.

00:49:09.423 --> 00:49:13.120
Inform Transporter Room Two
to beam the Governor aboard.

00:49:13.160 --> 00:49:16.095
I must make one thing
very clear, Jean-Luc.

00:49:16.130 --> 00:49:18.064
If we run into
any serious opposition

00:49:18.098 --> 00:49:20.498
I'm taking us back
into Federation territory.

00:49:20.534 --> 00:49:24.402
We aren't well-armed and
wouldn't last long in a fight.

00:49:24.438 --> 00:49:26.633
Governor Worf is aboard,
Captain.

00:49:26.673 --> 00:49:27.970
All right.

00:49:28.008 --> 00:49:30.306
Set course
for the Devron system.

00:49:30.344 --> 00:49:31.675
Warp 13.

00:49:34.548 --> 00:49:38.177
Once more,
for old time's sake?

00:49:48.028 --> 00:49:49.586
Engage.

00:49:49.630 --> 00:49:51.598
Engage to where, sir?

00:49:51.632 --> 00:49:54.726
Uh, set a course
for the Devron system

00:49:54.768 --> 00:49:56.759
and engage at warp nine.

00:49:56.804 --> 00:49:59.102
The Devron system is inside
the Neutral Zone, sir.

00:49:59.139 --> 00:50:00.766
I am aware of that, Lieutenant.

00:50:00.808 --> 00:50:01.866
Carry out my orders, Chief.

00:50:01.942 --> 00:50:03.432
Aye, sir.

00:50:03.477 --> 00:50:05.809
Captain, may I have a word
with you in private?

00:50:05.846 --> 00:50:07.245
Yes, of course, Counselor.

00:50:07.281 --> 00:50:08.475
Contact Farpoint Station.

00:50:08.515 --> 00:50:10.574
I wish to speak
with Commander Riker.

00:50:10.617 --> 00:50:12.744
Aye, sir.

00:50:17.391 --> 00:50:20.588
Captain, I just wanted
to voice my concerns

00:50:20.627 --> 00:50:23.255
about the way
the crew is responding

00:50:23.297 --> 00:50:25.288
to your unexpected orders.

00:50:25.332 --> 00:50:26.629
They don't trust me.

00:50:26.667 --> 00:50:28.692
They think
that I'm behaving erratically.

00:50:28.735 --> 00:50:29.997
Some do.

00:50:30.037 --> 00:50:31.299
Others are confused.

00:50:31.338 --> 00:50:33.397
It takes some time
for a new crew

00:50:33.440 --> 00:50:35.237
to get to know their Captain

00:50:35.275 --> 00:50:36.469
and for him to know them.

00:50:36.510 --> 00:50:37.909
I understand, but I also know

00:50:37.978 --> 00:50:40.446
what this crew is capable of,
even if they don't.

00:50:40.481 --> 00:50:43.746
It would also help
if they knew what was going on.

00:50:43.784 --> 00:50:46.309
I know it's difficult
operating in the dark

00:50:46.353 --> 00:50:49.481
but, right now, I don't think
I have any other choice.

00:50:49.523 --> 00:50:51.491
Yar to Captain Picard.

00:50:51.525 --> 00:50:54.016
I have Commander Riker
for you, sir.

00:50:54.061 --> 00:50:55.824
Excuse me.

00:50:55.863 --> 00:50:57.922
Put him through here.

00:50:59.166 --> 00:51:00.895
Commander Riker,
I wanted to inform you

00:51:00.934 --> 00:51:02.765
that we will be delayed
picking you up

00:51:02.803 --> 00:51:04.270
at Farpoint Station.

00:51:04.304 --> 00:51:06.272
I see.
May I ask how long?

00:51:06.306 --> 00:51:07.273
I can't say.

00:51:07.307 --> 00:51:08.501
I'll keep you updated.

00:51:08.542 --> 00:51:09.975
Will you inform Dr. Crusher

00:51:10.010 --> 00:51:12.410
and Lieutenant La Forge
of our delay?

00:51:12.446 --> 00:51:13.413
Understood.

00:51:13.447 --> 00:51:14.675
Riker out.

00:51:17.284 --> 00:51:19.445
Is there anything else,
Counselor?

00:51:19.486 --> 00:51:22.216
Actually, sir, there is.

00:51:22.256 --> 00:51:25.316
I was debating
whether to mention it

00:51:25.359 --> 00:51:27.884
and perhaps...

00:51:27.995 --> 00:51:30.156
It's about Commander Riker.

00:51:30.197 --> 00:51:32.256
What about him?

00:51:32.299 --> 00:51:35.996
I think you should know
that he and I have had a...

00:51:36.036 --> 00:51:38.129
prior relationship.

00:51:38.171 --> 00:51:39.468
I see.

00:51:39.506 --> 00:51:42.441
Do you think this will
interfere with your duties?

00:51:42.476 --> 00:51:43.636
Not at all.

00:51:43.677 --> 00:51:45.167
It happened several years ago

00:51:45.212 --> 00:51:47.043
and it's well behind
both of us now.

00:51:47.080 --> 00:51:48.707
I just thought you should know.

00:51:48.749 --> 00:51:50.410
Well, I appreciate
your telling me

00:51:50.450 --> 00:51:52.145
but I'm quite sure
that the two of you

00:51:52.185 --> 00:51:54.278
will find some way
to deal with the situation.

00:51:54.321 --> 00:51:56.312
Thank you, sir.

00:52:05.432 --> 00:52:07.400
Tea, Earl Grey. Hot.

00:52:07.434 --> 00:52:10.460
That beverage
has not been programmed

00:52:10.504 --> 00:52:12.438
into the replication system.

00:52:12.472 --> 00:52:14.770
So, Captain...

00:52:14.808 --> 00:52:17.709
how long shall we
stare at each other

00:52:17.744 --> 00:52:19.712
across the Neutral Zone?

00:52:19.746 --> 00:52:23.477
There is an alternative,
Tomalak.

00:52:23.517 --> 00:52:25.644
We each know why we're here.

00:52:25.686 --> 00:52:29.087
We could each send one ship
into the Neutral Zone

00:52:29.122 --> 00:52:32.285
to investigate the anomaly
in the Devron system.

00:52:32.326 --> 00:52:35.124
Has Starfleet Command
approved this arrangement?

00:52:35.162 --> 00:52:36.094
No.

00:52:36.129 --> 00:52:37.596
I like it already.

00:52:37.631 --> 00:52:38.757
Agreed.

00:52:38.799 --> 00:52:40.767
One ship from each side.

00:52:40.801 --> 00:52:43.736
But I warn you,
if another Federation starship

00:52:43.770 --> 00:52:45.203
tries to enter the zone...

00:52:45.238 --> 00:52:46.603
There is no need
to make threats.

00:52:46.640 --> 00:52:48.335
We each know the consequences.

00:52:48.375 --> 00:52:50.104
Very well.

00:52:50.143 --> 00:52:53.476
I'll see you
in the Devron system.

00:52:54.514 --> 00:52:56.209
Helm, set a course
for the Devron system.

00:52:56.249 --> 00:52:57.216
Warp five.

00:52:57.250 --> 00:52:58.217
Aye, sir.

00:52:58.251 --> 00:52:59.240
Engage.

00:53:05.792 --> 00:53:09.319
Sensors are picking up
a large subspace anomaly

00:53:09.363 --> 00:53:11.024
directly ahead.

00:53:11.064 --> 00:53:12.588
All stop.

00:53:12.633 --> 00:53:13.964
On screen.

00:53:15.969 --> 00:53:17.834
Full scan, Mr. Data.

00:53:17.871 --> 00:53:19.133
Aye, sir.

00:53:19.172 --> 00:53:21.163
We have to get
as much information

00:53:21.208 --> 00:53:23.073
as possible about that anomaly.

00:53:23.110 --> 00:53:26.307
We are approaching
the Devron system, Captain.

00:53:26.346 --> 00:53:29.372
Sensors are picking up
a large subspace anomaly

00:53:29.416 --> 00:53:30.713
directly ahead.

00:53:30.751 --> 00:53:32.082
All stop.
On screen.

00:53:35.455 --> 00:53:38.253
Then it is larger in the past.

00:53:38.291 --> 00:53:39.417
Sir?

00:53:39.459 --> 00:53:40.824
Nothing.

00:53:40.861 --> 00:53:42.829
Full scan, Mr. Data.

00:53:42.863 --> 00:53:44.387
Aye, sir.

00:53:45.899 --> 00:53:48.265
On screen! On screen!
Let's see it!

00:53:59.746 --> 00:54:03.705
As you can see, sir,
there's nothing there.

00:54:09.623 --> 00:54:11.488
Still nothing, Captain.

00:54:11.524 --> 00:54:13.424
I've conducted
a full sensor sweep

00:54:13.460 --> 00:54:15.655
out to one light-year
from the Pasteur.

00:54:15.695 --> 00:54:16.855
No temporal anomalies

00:54:16.963 --> 00:54:18.863
no particle fluctuations,
nothing.

00:54:18.899 --> 00:54:20.025
I don't understand.

00:54:20.066 --> 00:54:21.966
It was here
in the other two time periods.

00:54:22.002 --> 00:54:23.629
Why isn't it here now?

00:54:23.670 --> 00:54:27.868
Captain, I have been monitoring
Klingon communications channels.

00:54:27.908 --> 00:54:30.433
Several warships
have been dispatched

00:54:30.477 --> 00:54:32.445
to this sector to search

00:54:32.479 --> 00:54:34.811
for a renegade
Federation vessel.

00:54:36.750 --> 00:54:38.445
You're not thinking of leaving?

00:54:38.485 --> 00:54:40.453
There's nothing here, Jean-Luc.

00:54:40.487 --> 00:54:42.978
But there should be.
There has to be!

00:54:43.023 --> 00:54:44.991
Data, is there some other way

00:54:45.025 --> 00:54:46.993
to scan for temporal
disturbances?

00:54:47.027 --> 00:54:49.996
Something that isn't covered
in a normal sensor sweep?

00:54:50.030 --> 00:54:51.190
There are several methods

00:54:51.231 --> 00:54:52.823
of detecting
temporal disturbances

00:54:52.866 --> 00:54:55.994
but we're limited
by the equipment on the Pasteur.

00:54:56.036 --> 00:54:58.664
We should head back
to Federation territory.

00:54:58.705 --> 00:55:02.106
However, it may be possible
to modify the main deflector

00:55:02.142 --> 00:55:04.440
to emit
an inverse tachyon pulse

00:55:04.477 --> 00:55:07.605
which could scan
beyond the subspace barrier.

00:55:07.647 --> 00:55:09.114
That's it.
Make it so.

00:55:09.149 --> 00:55:10.673
Wait a minute.

00:55:10.717 --> 00:55:13.117
Data, how long would this take?

00:55:13.153 --> 00:55:14.415
To make the modifications

00:55:14.454 --> 00:55:16.183
and search
the entire Devron system

00:55:16.222 --> 00:55:17.951
would take
approximately 14 hours.

00:55:17.991 --> 00:55:19.219
All right.

00:55:19.259 --> 00:55:21.124
Data, begin to modify
the tachyon pulse.

00:55:21.161 --> 00:55:24.619
Ensign Chilton, lay in a course
back to the Federation.

00:55:24.664 --> 00:55:26.188
We'll stay here
for six more hours.

00:55:26.232 --> 00:55:27.631
And if we haven't found anything

00:55:27.667 --> 00:55:29.134
we're heading back,
maximum warp.

00:55:29.169 --> 00:55:30.466
Aye, sir.

00:55:30.503 --> 00:55:32.801
But six more hours
may not be enough.

00:55:32.839 --> 00:55:34.807
We have to stay here
until we find it

00:55:34.841 --> 00:55:36.468
no matter how long it takes.

00:55:36.509 --> 00:55:38.306
Carry out my orders.

00:55:38.345 --> 00:55:40.677
May I see you a moment?

00:55:46.386 --> 00:55:47.876
Beverly, I cannot believe

00:55:47.921 --> 00:55:50.219
that you are not willing
to stay here until we...

00:55:50.256 --> 00:55:51.655
Don't you ever question

00:55:51.691 --> 00:55:54.125
my orders on the Bridge
of my ship again.

00:55:54.160 --> 00:55:55.991
Damn it!
I was just trying to...

00:55:56.029 --> 00:55:58.190
Look, there are
larger concerns here.

00:55:58.231 --> 00:56:00.131
What you don't understand is...

00:56:00.166 --> 00:56:01.963
I understand that you
would never have

00:56:02.002 --> 00:56:03.526
tolerated that kind of behavior

00:56:03.570 --> 00:56:05.629
back on the Enterprise,
and I won't here.

00:56:05.672 --> 00:56:08.402
I don't care if you're
my ex-Captain or my ex-husband.

00:56:10.977 --> 00:56:12.103
You're right.

00:56:12.145 --> 00:56:13.772
I was out of line.

00:56:13.813 --> 00:56:15.280
It won't happen again.

00:56:15.315 --> 00:56:17.374
But what you have
to understand is

00:56:17.417 --> 00:56:18.816
what is at stake here.

00:56:18.852 --> 00:56:21.446
Q has said that all of humanity
will be destroyed.

00:56:21.488 --> 00:56:22.853
I know.

00:56:22.922 --> 00:56:25.857
That's why I've allowed
us to stay here longer

00:56:25.959 --> 00:56:28.257
and keep looking.

00:56:28.294 --> 00:56:31.627
But I also want you
to allow for the possibility

00:56:31.664 --> 00:56:34.155
that none of what you're saying
is real.

00:56:34.200 --> 00:56:35.360
What?

00:56:37.504 --> 00:56:39.802
Jean-Luc, I care
for you too much

00:56:39.839 --> 00:56:41.739
not to tell you the truth.

00:56:41.775 --> 00:56:45.836
You have advanced
Irumodic Syndrome.

00:56:45.879 --> 00:56:49.508
It's possible that all
of this is in your mind.

00:56:56.589 --> 00:57:02.289
I'll stay here six hours longer
and then we're heading home.

00:57:04.631 --> 00:57:07.429
I want you to remember...

00:57:07.467 --> 00:57:13.963
if it were anyone else but you,
we wouldn't even be here.

00:57:22.549 --> 00:57:25.575
Eh? What was that she said,
sonny?

00:57:25.618 --> 00:57:27.483
I couldn't quite hear her.

00:57:27.520 --> 00:57:28.987
Q?

00:57:29.022 --> 00:57:31.490
What is going on here?

00:57:31.524 --> 00:57:33.856
Where is the anomaly?

00:57:33.960 --> 00:57:35.359
Where's your mommy?

00:57:35.395 --> 00:57:36.623
Well, I don't know.

00:57:36.663 --> 00:57:37.789
Answer me!

00:57:40.333 --> 00:57:42.961
There is an answer, Jean-Luc

00:57:43.002 --> 00:57:45.664
but I can't hand it to you.

00:57:45.705 --> 00:57:47.866
Although you do have help.

00:57:47.907 --> 00:57:49.465
What help?

00:57:49.509 --> 00:57:51.875
You're not alone, you know.

00:57:51.978 --> 00:57:56.642
What you were,
and what you are to become

00:57:56.683 --> 00:57:59.516
will always be with you.

00:57:59.552 --> 00:58:01.179
My time shifting...

00:58:01.221 --> 00:58:03.815
the answer does lie there,
doesn't it?

00:58:03.923 --> 00:58:06.414
Now, tell me one thing.

00:58:06.459 --> 00:58:11.487
This anomaly we're looking for
will that destroy humanity?

00:58:11.531 --> 00:58:13.499
You're forgetting, Jean-Luc.

00:58:15.268 --> 00:58:17.463
You destroy humanity.

00:58:17.504 --> 00:58:20.803
By-by doing what?

00:58:20.840 --> 00:58:22.000
When?

00:58:22.041 --> 00:58:24.407
How can...?

00:58:25.879 --> 00:58:27.312
Report, Mr. Data.

00:58:27.347 --> 00:58:31.283
The anomaly is 200 million
kilometers in diameter.

00:58:31.317 --> 00:58:33.285
It is a highly-focused
temporal energy source

00:58:33.319 --> 00:58:36.447
which is emitting approximately
the same energy output

00:58:36.489 --> 00:58:37.956
as ten G-type stars.

00:58:37.991 --> 00:58:40.289
What is the source
of this energy?

00:58:40.326 --> 00:58:41.793
I am uncertain, sir.

00:58:41.828 --> 00:58:44.296
Sensors are unable
to penetrate the anomaly.

00:58:44.330 --> 00:58:46.798
What if we modified
the main deflector

00:58:46.833 --> 00:58:48.960
to emit an inverse tachyon pulse

00:58:49.002 --> 00:58:52.130
that might be able to scan
beyond the subspace barrier?

00:58:52.172 --> 00:58:54.003
That might give us some idea

00:58:54.040 --> 00:58:57.476
of what the interior
of this thing looks like.

00:58:57.510 --> 00:58:59.808
That is
a most intriguing idea, sir.

00:58:59.846 --> 00:59:04.249
I do not believe a tachyon beam
was ever used in such a way.

00:59:04.284 --> 00:59:06.946
I had no idea you were so versed

00:59:06.986 --> 00:59:09.250
in the intricacies
of temporal theory, sir.

00:59:09.289 --> 00:59:12.452
I have some friends
who are well-versed in it.

00:59:12.492 --> 00:59:13.823
Make it so.

00:59:13.893 --> 00:59:17.260
I believe we can make
the necessary modifications

00:59:17.297 --> 00:59:19.128
in Main Engineering, sir.

00:59:21.868 --> 00:59:23.460
We can get more power
if we reroute

00:59:23.503 --> 00:59:25.835
the primary EPS taps
to the deflector array.

00:59:25.939 --> 00:59:27.634
Agreed.

00:59:34.080 --> 00:59:36.344
Initiating tachyon pulse.

00:59:41.387 --> 00:59:43.582
Okay.

00:59:43.623 --> 00:59:45.250
The pulse is holding steady.

00:59:45.291 --> 00:59:47.122
We're starting to receive data
from the scan.

00:59:47.160 --> 00:59:49.594
It will take the computer
some time to give us

00:59:49.629 --> 00:59:51.688
a complete picture
of the anomaly's interior.

00:59:51.731 --> 00:59:52.720
I suggest we...

00:59:53.766 --> 00:59:54.733
Geordi?

00:59:54.767 --> 00:59:55.734
Oh!

00:59:55.768 --> 00:59:56.792
What is wrong?

00:59:56.836 --> 00:59:58.303
I don't know.

00:59:58.338 --> 01:00:02.172
It's like somebody's sticking
an ice pick in my temples.

01:00:02.208 --> 01:00:04.176
Hmm...

01:00:04.210 --> 01:00:06.303
My VISOR's picking up

01:00:06.346 --> 01:00:08.974
all kinds of electromagnetic
fluctuations.

01:00:09.015 --> 01:00:10.312
Data to Sick Bay.

01:00:10.350 --> 01:00:12.284
Medical emergency
in Main Engineering.

01:00:15.321 --> 01:00:17.846
This is amazing.

01:00:17.890 --> 01:00:20.484
The DNA in his optic nerves
is regenerating.

01:00:20.526 --> 01:00:24.360
Geordi, it's as if
you're growing new eyes.

01:00:24.397 --> 01:00:25.659
How is this possible?

01:00:25.698 --> 01:00:27.256
It shouldn't be possible at all.

01:00:27.300 --> 01:00:29.234
There's no medical explanation

01:00:29.269 --> 01:00:32.067
for spontaneous regeneration
of an organ.

01:00:32.105 --> 01:00:35.040
Doctor, we've just gotten
reports from two crew members

01:00:35.074 --> 01:00:36.541
who say they have old scars

01:00:36.576 --> 01:00:38.601
which are healing themselves.

01:00:38.645 --> 01:00:42.240
Captain, I believe I have
a partial explanation.

01:00:42.282 --> 01:00:45.012
I have completed my analysis
of the anomaly.

01:00:45.051 --> 01:00:47.679
It appears to be a multiphasic
temporal convergence

01:00:47.720 --> 01:00:49.381
in the space-time continuum.

01:00:49.422 --> 01:00:51.287
In English, Data.

01:00:51.324 --> 01:00:55.761
It is, in essence,
an eruption of anti-time.

01:00:55.795 --> 01:00:57.092
Anti-time?

01:00:57.130 --> 01:01:00.190
A relatively new concept
in temporal mechanics.

01:01:00.233 --> 01:01:02.326
The relationship between
anti-time and normal time

01:01:02.368 --> 01:01:05.531
is analogous to the relationship
between anti-matter

01:01:05.571 --> 01:01:07.163
and normal matter.

01:01:07.206 --> 01:01:11.267
So, if time and anti-time
were to collide...?

01:01:11.311 --> 01:01:13.279
They would annihilate
one another

01:01:13.313 --> 01:01:14.871
causing a rupture in space.

01:01:14.947 --> 01:01:18.178
I believe this is what happened
in the Devron system.

01:01:18.217 --> 01:01:21.482
The rupture may be sending out
waves of temporal energy

01:01:21.521 --> 01:01:23.853
which are disrupting
the normal flow of time.

01:01:23.890 --> 01:01:25.380
Data, what could have caused

01:01:25.425 --> 01:01:27.757
this collision
of time and anti-time?

01:01:27.794 --> 01:01:30.092
"Anti-time," sir?

01:01:30.129 --> 01:01:33.826
I believe that if you modify
the deflectors to send out

01:01:33.866 --> 01:01:36.164
an inverse tachyon pulse,
then you'll find

01:01:36.202 --> 01:01:39.831
that the anomaly is a rupture
between time and anti-time.

01:01:39.872 --> 01:01:41.999
That is a fascinating
hypothesis.

01:01:42.041 --> 01:01:43.167
How did you find...?

01:01:43.209 --> 01:01:45.507
I don't have time
to discuss it now, Mr. Data.

01:01:45.545 --> 01:01:48.514
Do the modifications,
and send out the pulse.

01:01:48.548 --> 01:01:52.006
Then try working on a theory
as to what caused this rupture.

01:01:52.051 --> 01:01:54.747
Mr. O'Brien,
how large is this anomaly?

01:01:54.787 --> 01:01:55.913
Approximately

01:01:56.022 --> 01:01:58.422
400 million kilometers
in diameter, sir.

01:01:58.458 --> 01:02:03.191
I don't understand
why it's bigger in the past.

01:02:03.229 --> 01:02:05.129
Lieutenant, you have the Bridge.

01:02:05.164 --> 01:02:06.631
I'll be in my ready room.

01:02:06.666 --> 01:02:08.190
Aye, sir.

01:02:10.536 --> 01:02:12.003
What's going on?

01:02:12.038 --> 01:02:13.972
We're under attack.

01:02:14.006 --> 01:02:15.564
Shield strength down to 52%.

01:02:15.608 --> 01:02:18.441
Minor damage
to the port nacelle.

01:02:18.478 --> 01:02:20.207
Two Klingon attack cruisers

01:02:20.246 --> 01:02:22.339
decloaking to port
and starboard.

01:02:33.026 --> 01:02:35.790
Warp speed.
Get us out of here.

01:02:35.828 --> 01:02:39.457
Warp power's off-line, sir.

01:02:40.700 --> 01:02:42.565
Heading 148, mark 215.

01:02:42.602 --> 01:02:44.661
Full impulse.

01:02:48.107 --> 01:02:49.904
Impulse power's fluctuating.

01:02:49.943 --> 01:02:51.376
Shields down to 30%.

01:02:51.411 --> 01:02:52.878
Weapons status.

01:02:52.912 --> 01:02:55.642
These weapons are no match
for their shields.

01:02:55.682 --> 01:02:58.810
Geordi, we need
more warp power... now.

01:02:58.851 --> 01:03:01.012
I'm trying, Captain.
They're too much for us.

01:03:01.054 --> 01:03:03.045
I can't keep the phase
inducers on line.

01:03:07.327 --> 01:03:09.124
Shields down to nine percent.

01:03:09.162 --> 01:03:10.857
One more hit,
and they'll collapse.

01:03:10.897 --> 01:03:12.626
Open a channel.

01:03:12.665 --> 01:03:13.689
Open.

01:03:13.733 --> 01:03:16.293
This is Captain Beverly Picard.

01:03:16.336 --> 01:03:19.305
We are a medical ship
on a mission of mercy.

01:03:19.339 --> 01:03:21.273
Please break off all...

01:03:23.476 --> 01:03:25.706
Worf, signal our surrender.

01:03:32.719 --> 01:03:34.744
Tos Vah'cha do Worf.

01:03:34.787 --> 01:03:36.584
Do'lo jegh!

01:03:50.403 --> 01:03:52.735
Our shields have collapsed.
We are defenseless.

01:03:52.772 --> 01:03:54.137
Captain?

01:03:54.173 --> 01:03:55.606
Another ship is decloaking...

01:03:55.641 --> 01:03:58.109
bearing 215, mark 310.

01:03:58.144 --> 01:04:00.738
It's the Enterprise.

01:04:07.120 --> 01:04:08.348
They're hailing us.

01:04:08.388 --> 01:04:10.481
On screen.

01:04:10.523 --> 01:04:12.855
I had a feeling you weren't
going to listen to me.

01:04:12.892 --> 01:04:14.086
Stand by.

01:04:14.127 --> 01:04:16.527
I'll see if I can get
the Klingons' attention.

01:04:29.075 --> 01:04:30.702
The Enterprise is drawing
their fire.

01:04:30.743 --> 01:04:32.608
Damage report.

01:04:32.645 --> 01:04:34.704
The warp core
has been badly damaged.

01:04:34.747 --> 01:04:36.612
There's a breach in progress.

01:04:36.649 --> 01:04:38.173
We have to stop it.

01:04:38.217 --> 01:04:40.617
The Klingon ship is disengaging.

01:04:40.653 --> 01:04:42.484
Admiral Riker is hailing us.

01:04:42.522 --> 01:04:44.387
Our sensors indicate
your ship has

01:04:44.424 --> 01:04:46.187
a warp core breach in progress.

01:04:46.225 --> 01:04:48.022
Prepare for emergency beam-out.

01:04:57.136 --> 01:04:59.570
All the Pasteur's crew are
safely on board, Admiral.

01:04:59.605 --> 01:05:01.835
Raise the shields.
Where are the Klingons?

01:05:01.908 --> 01:05:03.535
They're still moving off, sir.

01:05:03.576 --> 01:05:04.838
Half a light-year away.

01:05:04.944 --> 01:05:06.241
They'll be back.

01:05:06.279 --> 01:05:07.439
As I said, I figured

01:05:07.480 --> 01:05:09.471
you wouldn't take no
for an answer.

01:05:09.515 --> 01:05:11.346
But I thought you had more sense

01:05:11.384 --> 01:05:14.182
than to send a defenseless ship
across the border

01:05:14.220 --> 01:05:16.245
into hostile territory
with no escort.

01:05:16.289 --> 01:05:18.189
If you had not turned down
the Captain

01:05:18.224 --> 01:05:19.691
when he came to you for help

01:05:19.725 --> 01:05:21.386
none of this
would have happened!

01:05:21.427 --> 01:05:23.725
But unlike you,
I still have a sense of honor

01:05:23.763 --> 01:05:24.855
and Ioyalty.

01:05:24.964 --> 01:05:26.261
We don't have time for this!

01:05:26.299 --> 01:05:28.062
The Pasteur's core
is going to breach!

01:05:30.236 --> 01:05:32.636
Take us out of here.

01:05:32.672 --> 01:05:35.106
Full impulse.

01:05:44.150 --> 01:05:46.710
All right,
let's get out of here.

01:05:46.752 --> 01:05:48.083
No, Will, we can't!

01:05:48.121 --> 01:05:49.679
We have to save humanity!

01:05:49.722 --> 01:05:50.984
Engage cloak.

01:05:51.023 --> 01:05:52.650
Admiral, we took a direct hit

01:05:52.692 --> 01:05:54.125
to the starboard plasma coil.

01:05:54.160 --> 01:05:55.559
Our cloak isn't functioning.

01:05:55.595 --> 01:05:57.028
Engineering reports it'll be

01:05:57.063 --> 01:05:59.293
seven hours before
we can cloak again.

01:05:59.332 --> 01:06:01.493
Al right, we'll do it
the old-fashioned way.

01:06:01.534 --> 01:06:03.434
Set a course
for Federation space, warp 13.

01:06:03.469 --> 01:06:05.369
Will, don't leave.
We have to stay here

01:06:05.404 --> 01:06:07.838
and find out what is causing
the temporal anomaly!

01:06:07.874 --> 01:06:09.171
We can't stay, Captain.

01:06:09.208 --> 01:06:11.836
We have to.
Everything depends on it.

01:06:11.878 --> 01:06:12.845
We can't leave now.

01:06:12.912 --> 01:06:14.379
Please, listen to me!

01:06:25.358 --> 01:06:28.623
Your visual acuity is improving
by the hour, Geordi.

01:06:34.867 --> 01:06:36.994
I'm sorry, Alyssa.

01:06:37.036 --> 01:06:39.834
May I take another look?

01:06:39.872 --> 01:06:43.308
You'll have a little
tenderness for a few days.

01:06:43.342 --> 01:06:45.742
That's to be expected.

01:06:51.250 --> 01:06:52.547
Jean-Luc.

01:06:52.585 --> 01:06:56.021
I'll be right back, Alyssa.

01:06:59.859 --> 01:07:02.487
Alyssa lost the baby.

01:07:02.528 --> 01:07:04.826
I think it's
the same phenomenon

01:07:04.864 --> 01:07:06.491
that affected Geordi.

01:07:06.532 --> 01:07:09.228
Somehow, the temporal energy
from the anomaly

01:07:09.268 --> 01:07:11.327
caused the fetal tissue
to revert

01:07:11.370 --> 01:07:13.497
to an earlier stage
of development.

01:07:13.539 --> 01:07:16.531
It's as if the unborn child
began to grow younger

01:07:16.576 --> 01:07:19.807
until finally the DNA itself
began to break down.

01:07:19.845 --> 01:07:21.005
How is she?

01:07:21.047 --> 01:07:23.174
Physically, she's fine, for now.

01:07:23.216 --> 01:07:25.548
But if this
temporal reversion continues

01:07:25.585 --> 01:07:26.950
I don't think any of us

01:07:26.986 --> 01:07:29.181
are going to be fine
for much longer.

01:07:29.222 --> 01:07:31.656
So this is affecting
the entire crew.

01:07:31.691 --> 01:07:34.854
Our cellular structures
appear to be coalescing...

01:07:34.894 --> 01:07:36.657
reverting to earlier forms.

01:07:36.696 --> 01:07:37.856
In some cases

01:07:37.897 --> 01:07:40.365
this has caused
old injuries to be healed

01:07:40.399 --> 01:07:42.367
but the effect
is only temporary.

01:07:42.401 --> 01:07:45.199
Eventually,
it may kill all of us.

01:07:49.242 --> 01:07:51.767
We have to determine
how widespread this effect is.

01:07:51.811 --> 01:07:52.835
Contact Starbase 23.

01:07:52.878 --> 01:07:54.243
That's the nearest outpost.

01:07:54.280 --> 01:07:57.249
Have them check their personnel
to see if there are

01:07:57.283 --> 01:07:59.148
any signs of temporal reversion.

01:07:59.185 --> 01:08:00.379
Aye, sir.

01:08:00.419 --> 01:08:03.149
Mr. Data, how close are you
to completing the tachyon scan?

01:08:03.189 --> 01:08:05.487
Approximately one hour,
45 minutes, sir.

01:08:05.524 --> 01:08:06.991
Good. When it's done,
I want you

01:08:07.026 --> 01:08:09.085
to find some way
of collapsing this anomaly

01:08:09.128 --> 01:08:10.493
without making things worse.

01:08:10.529 --> 01:08:11.621
Give me a risk analysis

01:08:11.664 --> 01:08:13.495
of whatever solution
you come up with.

01:08:13.532 --> 01:08:14.658
Aye, sir.

01:08:14.700 --> 01:08:15.792
Dismissed.

01:08:24.377 --> 01:08:28.040
It's a pretty big decision,
Jean-Luc.

01:08:28.080 --> 01:08:31.345
Tinkering with an anomaly
you know nothing about.

01:08:31.384 --> 01:08:33.045
Trying to collapse it.

01:08:33.085 --> 01:08:34.416
Isn't that risky?

01:08:34.453 --> 01:08:37.149
Why? Will that cause
the destruction of mankind?

01:08:37.189 --> 01:08:38.588
Maybe.

01:08:38.624 --> 01:08:42.287
On the other hand,
maybe leaving it alone

01:08:42.328 --> 01:08:44.193
would be the wrong thing to do.

01:08:44.230 --> 01:08:47.427
It's a pretty big decision,
all right.

01:08:47.466 --> 01:08:50.458
Would it help to have
a different perspective?

01:08:52.571 --> 01:08:55.301
Welcome home.

01:08:55.341 --> 01:08:56.638
Home?

01:08:56.676 --> 01:08:59.372
Don't you recognize
your old stomping grounds?

01:08:59.412 --> 01:09:00.674
This is Earth...

01:09:00.713 --> 01:09:01.805
France, about, oh...

01:09:01.914 --> 01:09:04.041
three and a half
billion years ago.

01:09:04.083 --> 01:09:05.812
Give or take an eon or two.

01:09:05.851 --> 01:09:08.046
Smells awful, doesn't it?

01:09:08.087 --> 01:09:12.251
All that sulfur
and volcanic ash.

01:09:12.291 --> 01:09:14.657
I really must speak
to the maid.

01:09:14.694 --> 01:09:17.686
Q, is there any point
to all this?

01:09:17.730 --> 01:09:19.163
Look.

01:09:24.303 --> 01:09:27.534
So, the anomaly is here, too.

01:09:27.573 --> 01:09:29.268
At Earth.

01:09:29.308 --> 01:09:31.003
At this point in history

01:09:31.043 --> 01:09:36.003
the anomaly fills your entire
quadrant of the galaxy.

01:09:36.048 --> 01:09:39.017
The further back in time...

01:09:39.051 --> 01:09:41.645
the larger the anomaly.

01:09:44.690 --> 01:09:47.488
Come here.

01:09:47.526 --> 01:09:49.892
There's something
I want to show you.

01:09:51.430 --> 01:09:53.227
You see this?

01:09:53.265 --> 01:09:55.495
This is you.

01:09:55.534 --> 01:09:57.661
I'm serious.

01:09:57.703 --> 01:09:59.102
Right here...

01:09:59.138 --> 01:10:01.470
life is about to form
on this planet

01:10:01.507 --> 01:10:03.099
for the very first time.

01:10:03.142 --> 01:10:05.702
A group of amino acids
are about to combine

01:10:05.745 --> 01:10:07.645
to form the first protein.

01:10:07.680 --> 01:10:10.171
The building blocks...

01:10:11.684 --> 01:10:14.847
of what you call life.

01:10:16.288 --> 01:10:18.279
Strange, isn't it?

01:10:18.324 --> 01:10:22.590
Everything you know...
your entire civilization...

01:10:22.628 --> 01:10:27.497
it all begins right here
in this little pond of goo.

01:10:27.533 --> 01:10:30.593
Appropriate somehow, isn't it?

01:10:30.636 --> 01:10:32.604
Too bad you didn't bring
your microscope.

01:10:32.638 --> 01:10:34.572
It's really quite fascinating.
Oh, look!

01:10:34.607 --> 01:10:36.598
There they go.

01:10:36.642 --> 01:10:39.543
The amino acids
are moving closer

01:10:39.578 --> 01:10:41.773
and closer...

01:10:41.814 --> 01:10:43.873
and closer.

01:10:45.351 --> 01:10:47.012
Aw...

01:10:47.052 --> 01:10:49.646
nothing happened.

01:10:49.688 --> 01:10:51.451
See what you've done?

01:10:51.490 --> 01:10:57.087
Are you saying
that I caused the anomaly?

01:10:57.129 --> 01:11:00.428
And that the anomaly somehow

01:11:00.466 --> 01:11:04.527
disrupted the beginnings
of life on Earth?

01:11:06.605 --> 01:11:09.233
Congratulations.

01:11:24.389 --> 01:11:26.414
Let's concentrate
on how this anomaly

01:11:26.457 --> 01:11:28.584
was initially formed.
Speculation.

01:11:28.626 --> 01:11:30.560
Our tachyon pulse
has been unable

01:11:30.595 --> 01:11:32.358
to completely penetrate
the anomaly.

01:11:32.397 --> 01:11:34.991
If we had information
on the center of the phenomenon

01:11:35.033 --> 01:11:37.058
we might have a basis
for speculation.

01:11:37.101 --> 01:11:39.228
Is there any way
that we can scan the interior?

01:11:39.270 --> 01:11:40.760
I've tried everything I know.

01:11:40.805 --> 01:11:42.500
There's just
too much interference.

01:11:42.540 --> 01:11:44.701
There's nothing on board
that'll do the job.

01:11:44.742 --> 01:11:45.709
Do you know what could?

01:11:45.743 --> 01:11:48.576
In theory, a tomographic
imaging scanner

01:11:48.613 --> 01:11:50.911
capable of multiphasic
resolution

01:11:50.949 --> 01:11:53.918
would be able to penetrate
this much interference.

01:11:53.952 --> 01:11:55.249
The Daystrom Institute

01:11:55.286 --> 01:11:57.584
has been working
on such a device

01:11:57.622 --> 01:12:00.591
but it is still
only theoretical.

01:12:00.625 --> 01:12:03.753
Data, do we have a tomographic
imaging scanner on board?

01:12:03.795 --> 01:12:05.194
Yes, sir.

01:12:05.229 --> 01:12:08.596
Can you use it to scan
the interior of the anomaly?

01:12:08.633 --> 01:12:10.191
Possibly.

01:12:10.234 --> 01:12:12.293
There is a great deal
of interference

01:12:12.337 --> 01:12:14.635
but I am getting some readings.

01:12:14.672 --> 01:12:17.300
This is very unusual.

01:12:17.342 --> 01:12:18.639
What is it?

01:12:18.676 --> 01:12:20.837
It appears
that our tachyon pulse

01:12:20.878 --> 01:12:23.779
is converging
with two other tachyon pulses

01:12:23.815 --> 01:12:25.749
at the center of the anomaly.

01:12:25.783 --> 01:12:27.148
The two other pulses

01:12:27.185 --> 01:12:29.847
have the exact same
amplitude modulation

01:12:29.887 --> 01:12:31.149
as our own pulse.

01:12:31.189 --> 01:12:32.679
It is as if all three

01:12:32.724 --> 01:12:34.692
originated from the Enterprise.

01:12:34.726 --> 01:12:37.217
Three pulses...

01:12:37.261 --> 01:12:40.196
from three time periods

01:12:40.231 --> 01:12:43.860
converging
at one point in space.

01:12:43.901 --> 01:12:47.530
Captain, what are
you suggesting?

01:12:53.378 --> 01:12:55.903
Computer,
where is Admiral Riker?

01:12:55.980 --> 01:12:58.540
Admiral Riker is in Ten-Forward.

01:13:09.394 --> 01:13:12.192
The ship has held up
pretty well over the years.

01:13:12.230 --> 01:13:15.631
They tried to decommission her
about five years ago.

01:13:15.666 --> 01:13:18.760
One of the advantages
of being an Admiral

01:13:18.803 --> 01:13:21.067
is you get to choose
your own ship.

01:13:21.105 --> 01:13:22.572
Will?

01:13:22.607 --> 01:13:25.132
How long is this thing
between you and Worf

01:13:25.176 --> 01:13:26.768
going to go on?

01:13:26.811 --> 01:13:29.075
It's been going on
for over 20 years.

01:13:29.113 --> 01:13:33.209
Doesn't look like it's going
to end anytime soon.

01:13:33.251 --> 01:13:36.414
I suspect the last thing
Counselor Troi would have wanted

01:13:36.454 --> 01:13:38.479
is for the two of you
to be alienated.

01:13:38.523 --> 01:13:40.889
I agree.

01:13:40.992 --> 01:13:43.256
I think it's time
to put it behind you.

01:13:43.294 --> 01:13:46.286
I tried at Deanna's funeral.

01:13:46.330 --> 01:13:49.595
He wouldn't even talk with me.

01:13:49.634 --> 01:13:52.125
Might have been tough
for him then.

01:13:52.170 --> 01:13:54.695
He took her death pretty hard.

01:13:54.739 --> 01:13:56.832
Oh, yeah?

01:13:56.874 --> 01:13:58.865
Well, he wasn't the only one.

01:14:02.180 --> 01:14:06.344
I know, but I think, in his
mind, you were the reason

01:14:06.384 --> 01:14:09.376
that he and Deanna
never got together.

01:14:09.420 --> 01:14:11.752
I never did anything
to stand in his way.

01:14:11.789 --> 01:14:14.451
Didn't you, Will?

01:14:17.328 --> 01:14:19.455
Did I?

01:14:21.399 --> 01:14:23.731
I didn't want to admit
that it was over.

01:14:27.305 --> 01:14:31.071
I always thought that we
would get together again.

01:14:31.109 --> 01:14:33.100
And then she was gone.

01:14:35.313 --> 01:14:39.579
You think you have all the time
in the world, until...

01:14:39.617 --> 01:14:41.710
Yeah.

01:14:55.566 --> 01:14:56.897
Ensign...

01:14:56.968 --> 01:14:59.903
how do I get to Ten-Forward?

01:14:59.937 --> 01:15:03.634
It's four decks down, sir.
Section 005.

01:15:03.674 --> 01:15:05.437
Thank you.

01:15:20.124 --> 01:15:21.785
Oh, my God.

01:15:21.826 --> 01:15:23.623
Will...

01:15:23.661 --> 01:15:25.390
Will, I know why it's happening.

01:15:25.429 --> 01:15:27.556
I know what's causing
the anomaly.

01:15:27.598 --> 01:15:28.826
We have to go back.

01:15:28.866 --> 01:15:31.733
The only place we're going
back to, sir, is bed.

01:15:31.769 --> 01:15:34.602
Damn it, Will, I know
why it's happening!

01:15:34.639 --> 01:15:37.130
We caused the anomaly
with the tachyon pulse.

01:15:37.175 --> 01:15:38.836
It happened three times, Will.

01:15:38.876 --> 01:15:41.140
We did it
in three different time periods.

01:15:41.179 --> 01:15:43.647
I think you better come with me.

01:15:43.681 --> 01:15:45.410
Will you leave me alone?

01:15:45.449 --> 01:15:47.212
Damn it, I'm not stupid!

01:15:47.251 --> 01:15:49.742
Will, the tachyon pulses...
they were used

01:15:49.787 --> 01:15:53.348
in the same spot in three
different time periods.

01:15:53.391 --> 01:15:54.722
Don't you see?

01:15:54.759 --> 01:15:57.057
Wh-when the tachyon pulse
used...

01:15:57.094 --> 01:15:58.288
I mean, uh...

01:15:58.329 --> 01:16:00.593
I mean, when the Pasteur

01:16:00.631 --> 01:16:03.099
used the tachyon pulse,
then, then...

01:16:03.134 --> 01:16:04.499
we, uh...

01:16:04.535 --> 01:16:06.435
I mean, everything started,
Will.

01:16:06.470 --> 01:16:08.165
We-we set everything in motion.

01:16:08.206 --> 01:16:11.334
It... it's like the
chicken and the egg, Will.

01:16:11.375 --> 01:16:13.138
The chicken and the egg!

01:16:13.177 --> 01:16:17.079
We think it started
in the past, but it didn't.

01:16:17.114 --> 01:16:20.140
It started right here,
in the future.

01:16:20.184 --> 01:16:23.119
That's why it's getting
larger in the past.

01:16:23.154 --> 01:16:25.714
I think I know what the Captain
is talking about.

01:16:25.756 --> 01:16:29.556
If I'm not mistaken,
he's describing a paradox.

01:16:29.594 --> 01:16:31.528
Yes! Right, that's it.

01:16:31.562 --> 01:16:32.654
Intriguing.

01:16:32.697 --> 01:16:34.096
It is possible...

01:16:34.131 --> 01:16:37.589
We could have caused
the very anomaly

01:16:37.635 --> 01:16:39.762
we have been looking for.

01:16:39.804 --> 01:16:41.704
Let us assume for a moment

01:16:41.739 --> 01:16:45.573
that the Captain has been
traveling through time.

01:16:45.610 --> 01:16:49.137
Let us also assume
he has initiated a tachyon pulse

01:16:49.180 --> 01:16:53.310
at the same coordinates
in all three time periods.

01:16:53.351 --> 01:16:55.512
In that case, it is possible

01:16:55.553 --> 01:16:58.886
that the convergence
of three tachyon pulses

01:16:58.956 --> 01:17:01.186
could have ruptured
the subspace barrier

01:17:01.225 --> 01:17:03.284
and created
an anti-time reaction.

01:17:03.327 --> 01:17:05.261
I see
where you're going, Data.

01:17:05.296 --> 01:17:07.127
And because anti-time operates

01:17:07.164 --> 01:17:09.223
opposite the way
normal time does

01:17:09.267 --> 01:17:11.394
the effects
would travel backwards

01:17:11.435 --> 01:17:12.834
through the space-time
continuum.

01:17:12.903 --> 01:17:14.734
Yes! That's why it gets
larger in the past.

01:17:14.772 --> 01:17:16.535
It grows as it travels
backwards in time.

01:17:16.574 --> 01:17:17.836
All right, just for the moment

01:17:17.908 --> 01:17:18.840
let's say that you're right.

01:17:18.943 --> 01:17:19.967
What do we do?

01:17:20.011 --> 01:17:22.309
Back, Will... we go back
to the Devron system.

01:17:22.346 --> 01:17:23.711
He may be right.

01:17:23.748 --> 01:17:25.978
If we go back
to the Devron system now

01:17:26.017 --> 01:17:27.609
we might be able to see

01:17:27.652 --> 01:17:30.382
the initial formation
of the anomaly.

01:17:32.189 --> 01:17:33.451
Riker to Bridge.

01:17:33.491 --> 01:17:36.949
Set a course for
the Devron system, maximum warp.

01:17:36.994 --> 01:17:38.188
Aye, sir.

01:17:44.802 --> 01:17:47.236
Worf, we could use a hand.

01:18:01.184 --> 01:18:03.152
Entering the Devron system, sir.

01:18:03.186 --> 01:18:04.653
Full stop.

01:18:04.688 --> 01:18:06.246
Sensors are picking up

01:18:06.290 --> 01:18:09.157
a small temporal anomaly
off the port bow.

01:18:09.192 --> 01:18:11.023
On screen.

01:18:16.166 --> 01:18:17.997
I was right.

01:18:18.035 --> 01:18:21.004
It's an anti-time eruption.

01:18:21.038 --> 01:18:23.598
It seems to have been formed
within the last six hours.

01:18:23.640 --> 01:18:25.039
We must stop it here

01:18:25.075 --> 01:18:27.373
so that it can't travel
back through time.

01:18:27.411 --> 01:18:30.209
Mr. Data, we need a solution
and we need it now.

01:18:30.247 --> 01:18:34.183
The anomaly is being sustained
by the continuing tachyon pulses

01:18:34.217 --> 01:18:35.980
from the other two time periods.

01:18:36.019 --> 01:18:37.247
I suggest shutting them down.

01:18:37.287 --> 01:18:39.653
The next time I'm there,
it's the first thing I'll do.

01:18:39.690 --> 01:18:41.521
Isn't there something
more we can do here?

01:18:41.558 --> 01:18:42.684
Seal the rupture somehow?

01:18:42.726 --> 01:18:44.523
I'll investigate the options.

01:18:45.796 --> 01:18:47.320
Data, disengage
the tachyon pulse.

01:18:47.364 --> 01:18:48.331
Sir?

01:18:48.365 --> 01:18:49.491
Do it!

01:18:49.533 --> 01:18:51.023
The convergence
of the tachyon pulses

01:18:51.068 --> 01:18:53.536
from the three time periods
is what is causing the anomaly.

01:18:53.570 --> 01:18:55.834
Aye, sir.

01:18:59.876 --> 01:19:01.776
Is there any change
in the anomaly?

01:19:01.812 --> 01:19:02.972
No, sir.

01:19:03.013 --> 01:19:05.379
Disengage the tachyon pulse.

01:19:05.415 --> 01:19:08.282
But we haven't finished
the scan, sir.

01:19:08.318 --> 01:19:09.615
I know that.

01:19:09.653 --> 01:19:11.120
But it is imperative

01:19:11.154 --> 01:19:14.123
that you disengage
the tachyon pulse immediately.

01:19:14.157 --> 01:19:15.488
Aye, sir.
Disengaging.

01:19:18.528 --> 01:19:20.189
Why isn't the anomaly
being affected?

01:19:20.230 --> 01:19:22.721
Why would it be, sir?

01:19:24.468 --> 01:19:27.562
I've shut off the tachyon pulses
in the other two time periods

01:19:27.604 --> 01:19:29.572
but it hasn't changed
the anomaly.

01:19:29.606 --> 01:19:31.506
It remains unaffected
here, as well, sir.

01:19:31.541 --> 01:19:32.530
What do we do?

01:19:32.576 --> 01:19:34.203
The only way to stop this thing

01:19:34.244 --> 01:19:36.212
is to repair the rupture
at the focal point

01:19:36.246 --> 01:19:38.077
where time and anti-time
are converging.

01:19:38.115 --> 01:19:39.241
How do we do that?

01:19:39.282 --> 01:19:40.579
It would require

01:19:40.617 --> 01:19:42.676
taking the ship into
the anomaly itself.

01:19:42.719 --> 01:19:44.710
Once inside, we may be able
to use the engines

01:19:44.755 --> 01:19:46.086
to create a static warp shell.

01:19:46.123 --> 01:19:47.647
Yeah, Data, that's right.

01:19:47.691 --> 01:19:48.851
And the shell would act

01:19:48.892 --> 01:19:50.519
as an artificial
subspace barrier

01:19:50.560 --> 01:19:52.050
separating time and anti-time.

01:19:52.095 --> 01:19:53.062
Collapsing the anomaly

01:19:53.096 --> 01:19:54.757
and restoring
the normal flow of time.

01:19:54.798 --> 01:19:56.095
But this would have to be done

01:19:56.133 --> 01:19:57.862
in the other two time periods,
as well.

01:19:57.901 --> 01:19:59.459
That could be a problem.

01:19:59.503 --> 01:20:02.028
The anomaly is so much larger
in the other two time periods.

01:20:02.072 --> 01:20:04.563
It may be dangerous
to take the ship in.

01:20:04.608 --> 01:20:06.337
Take the ship in where, sir?

01:20:06.376 --> 01:20:07.866
Into the anomaly, Chief.

01:20:07.944 --> 01:20:10.105
Lay in a course
for the exact center

01:20:10.147 --> 01:20:13.116
and transfer all available power
to the shields.

01:20:13.150 --> 01:20:15.414
Sir, can you give us
some explanation?

01:20:15.452 --> 01:20:17.386
No, Lieutenant, I cannot.

01:20:17.421 --> 01:20:20.151
Captain, so far,
we've obeyed every order

01:20:20.190 --> 01:20:22.818
no matter how farfetched
it might have seemed

01:20:22.859 --> 01:20:25.453
but if we're to risk
the safety of the ship and crew

01:20:25.495 --> 01:20:29.056
I think we have to ask you
for an explanation.

01:20:29.099 --> 01:20:31.431
I understand your concerns,
Lieutenant.

01:20:31.468 --> 01:20:34.062
And I know
that if I were in your position

01:20:34.104 --> 01:20:37.437
I would be doing the same
thing... looking for answers.

01:20:37.474 --> 01:20:39.408
But you're not going to find any

01:20:39.443 --> 01:20:42.606
because I don't have any
to give you.

01:20:42.646 --> 01:20:46.207
I know it is difficult
for you to understand

01:20:46.249 --> 01:20:48.581
but we have to take the ship

01:20:48.618 --> 01:20:51.678
into the very center
of the phenomenon

01:20:51.721 --> 01:20:54.212
and create a static warp shell.

01:20:54.257 --> 01:20:57.158
Now, this will put
the ship at risk.

01:20:57.194 --> 01:20:59.924
Quite frankly,
we may not survive.

01:20:59.996 --> 01:21:02.260
But I want you to believe
that I'm doing this

01:21:02.299 --> 01:21:04.324
for a greater purpose

01:21:04.367 --> 01:21:06.164
and that what is at stake here

01:21:06.203 --> 01:21:09.604
is more than any of you
can possibly imagine.

01:21:11.274 --> 01:21:13.139
I know you have your doubts
about me...

01:21:13.176 --> 01:21:14.973
about each other...

01:21:15.011 --> 01:21:16.308
about the ship.

01:21:16.346 --> 01:21:17.643
All I can say is

01:21:17.681 --> 01:21:19.979
that although we have
only been together

01:21:20.016 --> 01:21:22.348
for a short time

01:21:22.385 --> 01:21:27.413
I know that you are
the finest crew in the fleet

01:21:27.457 --> 01:21:32.827
and I would trust
each of you with my life.

01:21:32.863 --> 01:21:37.800
So, I am asking you
for a leap of faith...

01:21:39.803 --> 01:21:41.794
and to trust me.

01:21:49.179 --> 01:21:50.908
Shields up, maximum strength.

01:21:50.981 --> 01:21:53.449
Boosting field integrity
to the warp nacelles.

01:21:53.483 --> 01:21:56.816
We may encounter shearing forces
once we enter the anomaly.

01:21:56.853 --> 01:21:59.321
I am preparing to initiate
a static warp shell.

01:21:59.356 --> 01:22:00.880
Course laid in, sir.

01:22:00.924 --> 01:22:03.324
All decks report ready, sir.

01:22:03.360 --> 01:22:05.828
Take us in, Chief.

01:22:05.862 --> 01:22:07.227
Captain, I have an idea.

01:22:07.264 --> 01:22:09.095
If we take the ship
to the center

01:22:09.132 --> 01:22:10.690
of the anomaly and create...

01:22:10.734 --> 01:22:12.361
...a static warp shell...

01:22:12.402 --> 01:22:14.962
It could repair the barrier
and collapse the anomaly.

01:22:15.005 --> 01:22:16.768
Yes, sir.

01:22:16.806 --> 01:22:18.865
Mr. Data, you are
a clever man...

01:22:18.942 --> 01:22:20.409
in any time period.

01:22:20.443 --> 01:22:22.070
Helm?

01:22:22.112 --> 01:22:23.977
Lay in a course
for the center of the anomaly

01:22:24.014 --> 01:22:25.879
and prepare to initiate
a static warp shell.

01:22:25.916 --> 01:22:26.883
Aye, sir.

01:22:26.917 --> 01:22:28.680
The other two Enterprises...

01:22:28.718 --> 01:22:30.083
they're on their way.

01:22:30.120 --> 01:22:31.348
Very well.

01:22:31.388 --> 01:22:32.878
Ensign, take us in.

01:22:37.928 --> 01:22:39.418
We're entering the anomaly, sir.

01:22:39.462 --> 01:22:41.259
All hands brace for impact.

01:22:41.298 --> 01:22:44.665
The temporal energy
is interfering with main power.

01:22:44.701 --> 01:22:45.429
Switching to...

01:22:45.468 --> 01:22:46.867
Auxiliary power!

01:22:46.903 --> 01:22:49.371
I'm having trouble keeping
the impulse engines on line.

01:22:49.406 --> 01:22:51.601
I've got power fluctuations
all across the board.

01:22:51.641 --> 01:22:53.336
Maintain course and speed.

01:22:53.376 --> 01:22:56.106
Mr. Data, how long
until we reach the center?

01:22:56.146 --> 01:22:58.114
At least 30 seconds, sir.

01:23:04.421 --> 01:23:06.048
We've entered the anomaly.

01:23:06.089 --> 01:23:08.080
We have reached the center, sir.

01:23:08.124 --> 01:23:10.058
Initiate warp shell.

01:23:10.093 --> 01:23:13.859
Initiating
static warp shell now.

01:23:13.930 --> 01:23:15.989
Is it having any effect?

01:23:16.032 --> 01:23:17.693
Something is happening.

01:23:17.734 --> 01:23:20.726
A new subspace barrier
appears to be forming.

01:23:20.770 --> 01:23:23.705
Captain, the sensors
are picking up two other ships.

01:23:45.862 --> 01:23:47.261
Captain,
it appears to be working.

01:23:47.297 --> 01:23:48.821
The anomaly
is beginning to collapse.

01:23:48.865 --> 01:23:50.355
I think...

01:23:50.400 --> 01:23:52.994
The temporal energy is rupturing
our warp containment system.

01:23:53.036 --> 01:23:54.594
We must eject the core.

01:23:54.638 --> 01:23:55.798
No. We have to maintain

01:23:55.839 --> 01:23:58.034
the static warp shell
as long as possible.

01:24:01.378 --> 01:24:03.141
We're losing containment,
Captain.

01:24:03.179 --> 01:24:05.079
I-I can't stop it.
It's going to...

01:24:08.351 --> 01:24:10.251
Transfer emergency power

01:24:10.287 --> 01:24:12.187
to the anti-matter
containment system.

01:24:12.222 --> 01:24:14.588
I'm trying, but there's
a lot of interference.

01:24:14.624 --> 01:24:16.990
The warp shell is definitely
having an effect, sir.

01:24:17.027 --> 01:24:18.392
The anomaly is collapsing.

01:24:18.428 --> 01:24:19.656
I can't hold it.

01:24:19.696 --> 01:24:21.789
The containment system is going.

01:24:21.831 --> 01:24:23.264
Maintain your position.

01:24:23.300 --> 01:24:24.392
Mr. La Forge...

01:24:28.505 --> 01:24:30.871
Both of the other ships
have been destroyed.

01:24:30.907 --> 01:24:33.205
Two down, one to go.

01:24:33.243 --> 01:24:34.540
Data, report.

01:24:34.577 --> 01:24:36.340
The anomaly is nearly collapsed.

01:24:36.379 --> 01:24:37.437
We're losing containment.

01:24:37.480 --> 01:24:38.777
Good-bye, Jean-Luc.

01:24:38.815 --> 01:24:40.077
I'm going to miss you.

01:24:40.116 --> 01:24:41.583
You had such potential.

01:24:41.618 --> 01:24:44.109
But then again, all good things
must come to an end.

01:24:44.154 --> 01:24:45.519
Containment field
is at critical!

01:24:45.555 --> 01:24:47.455
I'm losing it!

01:25:07.610 --> 01:25:11.102
The Continuum didn't think
you had it in you, Jean-Luc

01:25:11.147 --> 01:25:13.741
but I knew you did.

01:25:15.752 --> 01:25:18.118
Are you saying that it worked?

01:25:18.154 --> 01:25:20.122
We collapsed the anomaly?

01:25:20.156 --> 01:25:21.555
Is that all this meant to you?

01:25:21.591 --> 01:25:23.821
Just another spatial anomaly?

01:25:23.860 --> 01:25:25.293
Just another day at the office?

01:25:25.328 --> 01:25:26.454
Did it work?

01:25:26.496 --> 01:25:28.123
Well, you're here, aren't you?

01:25:28.164 --> 01:25:30.655
You're talking to me,
aren't you?

01:25:30.700 --> 01:25:32.133
What about my crew?

01:25:33.403 --> 01:25:35.303
"The anomaly...
my ship... my crew..."

01:25:35.338 --> 01:25:38.535
I suppose you're worried
about your fish, too.

01:25:38.574 --> 01:25:40.838
Well, if it puts
your mind at ease

01:25:40.877 --> 01:25:43.038
you've saved humanity...

01:25:43.079 --> 01:25:44.808
once again.

01:25:49.118 --> 01:25:51.313
Thank you.

01:25:51.354 --> 01:25:53.652
For what?

01:25:53.689 --> 01:25:56.783
You had a hand
in helping me get out of this.

01:25:58.795 --> 01:26:01.787
I was the one
that got you into it...

01:26:01.831 --> 01:26:04.527
a directive from the Continuum.

01:26:04.567 --> 01:26:07.559
The part about
the helping hand, though...

01:26:07.603 --> 01:26:09.434
was my idea.

01:26:16.746 --> 01:26:18.338
I sincerely hope

01:26:18.381 --> 01:26:21.646
that this is the last time
that I find myself here.

01:26:21.684 --> 01:26:25.279
You just don't get it,
do you, Jean-Luc?

01:26:25.321 --> 01:26:27.846
The trial never ends.

01:26:27.890 --> 01:26:30.859
We wanted to see
if you had the ability

01:26:30.960 --> 01:26:33.394
to expand your mind
and your horizons.

01:26:33.429 --> 01:26:36.227
And for one brief moment,
you did.

01:26:36.265 --> 01:26:38.233
When I realized the paradox.

01:26:38.267 --> 01:26:39.632
Exactly.

01:26:39.669 --> 01:26:42.160
For that one fraction
of a second

01:26:42.205 --> 01:26:46.039
you were open to options
you had never considered.

01:26:46.075 --> 01:26:49.135
That is the exploration
that awaits you.

01:26:49.178 --> 01:26:52.841
Not mapping stars
and studying nebulae

01:26:52.882 --> 01:26:58.616
but charting the unknown
possibilities of existence.

01:26:58.654 --> 01:27:01.418
Q, what is it that you're
trying to tell me?

01:27:08.798 --> 01:27:11.596
You'll find out.

01:27:11.634 --> 01:27:15.092
In any case, I'll be watching.

01:27:15.137 --> 01:27:16.502
And if you're very lucky

01:27:16.539 --> 01:27:20.236
I'll drop by to say hello
from time to time.

01:27:20.276 --> 01:27:25.304
See you... out there.

01:27:34.657 --> 01:27:37.023
Captain, are you all right?

01:27:37.059 --> 01:27:40.688
Mr. Worf, what's the date?

01:27:40.730 --> 01:27:43.028
Stardate 47988.

01:27:50.606 --> 01:27:52.096
Is something wrong, sir?

01:27:52.141 --> 01:27:54.109
No. No.

01:27:54.143 --> 01:27:55.872
No, uh...

01:27:55.945 --> 01:27:59.540
I, uh, I think
I'll get back to bed.

01:28:01.250 --> 01:28:02.808
I, uh...

01:28:02.885 --> 01:28:06.150
I could use some sleep.

01:28:11.928 --> 01:28:14.453
Captain's Log, supplemental.

01:28:14.497 --> 01:28:17.660
Starfleet Command reports
no unusual activity

01:28:17.700 --> 01:28:19.395
along the Neutral Zone

01:28:19.435 --> 01:28:21.835
and there is no sign
of a temporal anomaly.

01:28:21.871 --> 01:28:24.465
It would appear that I am
the only member of the crew

01:28:24.507 --> 01:28:27.476
to retain any knowledge
of the events I experienced.

01:28:27.510 --> 01:28:28.807
Take it.

01:28:28.844 --> 01:28:30.334
Anytime, Doctor.

01:28:32.348 --> 01:28:34.578
Four hands in a row.

01:28:34.617 --> 01:28:36.278
How does he do it?

01:28:36.319 --> 01:28:37.877
I cheat.

01:28:39.121 --> 01:28:40.247
I'm kidding.

01:28:42.024 --> 01:28:43.150
You know, I was thinking

01:28:43.192 --> 01:28:44.659
about what the Captain
told us all

01:28:44.694 --> 01:28:46.491
about the future...

01:28:46.529 --> 01:28:50.397
about how we all changed
and drifted apart.

01:28:50.433 --> 01:28:53.425
Why would he want to tell us
what's to come?

01:28:53.469 --> 01:28:55.835
It sure goes against everything
we've always heard

01:28:55.871 --> 01:28:57.998
about not polluting
the timeline, doesn't it?

01:28:58.040 --> 01:29:00.634
I believe, however,
this situation is unique.

01:29:00.676 --> 01:29:04.612
Since the anomaly did not occur,
there have already been changes

01:29:04.647 --> 01:29:06.808
in the way
this timeline is unfolding.

01:29:06.916 --> 01:29:10.044
The future we experience
will undoubtedly be different

01:29:10.086 --> 01:29:12.452
from the one
the Captain encountered.

01:29:12.488 --> 01:29:14.285
Maybe that's why he told us.

01:29:14.323 --> 01:29:16.587
Knowing what happens
in that future

01:29:16.626 --> 01:29:18.617
allows us to change things now

01:29:18.661 --> 01:29:20.822
so that some things
never happen.

01:29:23.299 --> 01:29:24.960
Agreed.

01:29:27.003 --> 01:29:28.334
Come in.

01:29:28.371 --> 01:29:30.100
Am I too late?

01:29:30.139 --> 01:29:31.436
Of course not.

01:29:31.474 --> 01:29:33.772
Pull up a chair.

01:29:33.809 --> 01:29:36.471
Five card draw, deuces wild.

01:29:38.648 --> 01:29:40.047
Come in.

01:29:46.889 --> 01:29:48.857
Is there a problem, sir?

01:29:48.891 --> 01:29:50.415
No. I, uh...

01:29:50.459 --> 01:29:52.859
I just thought
that I might, um...

01:29:52.928 --> 01:29:55.954
I might join you this evening.

01:29:55.998 --> 01:29:57.556
Uh, if there's room.

01:29:57.600 --> 01:29:58.862
Of course.

01:29:58.934 --> 01:30:00.265
Have a seat.

01:30:03.739 --> 01:30:05.036
Would you care to deal, sir?

01:30:06.409 --> 01:30:09.105
Oh, thank you, Mr. Data.

01:30:09.145 --> 01:30:10.544
Actually, I, uh...

01:30:10.579 --> 01:30:14.743
I used to be quite a card player
in my youth, you know.

01:30:27.196 --> 01:30:30.165
I should have done this
a long time ago.

01:30:32.001 --> 01:30:33.764
You were always welcome.

01:30:37.506 --> 01:30:39.133
So...

01:30:39.175 --> 01:30:41.677
five card stud, nothing wild...

01:30:41.810 --> 01:30:44.142
and the sky's the limit.
